account for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 объяснять (что-л. чем-л.); являться причиной (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[Т1 (often simple tenses) [ex]♦ Не could not account for his foolish mistake.
	Melting snow accounts for the regular spring floods in the valley.[/ex]
	\[[com]T4 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How do you account for losing such a large sum of money?[/ex]
	\[[com]T6a (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Can you account for why our team lost?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 also answer for давать отчёт о (чём-л.), особ. о денежных суммах или товарах, оставленных под чью-л. ответственность:[/trn]
	\[Т1 (to) (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ You have to account to Bead Office for any stamps that you use.
	All the men are present or accounted for, sir.[/ex]
	\[[com]T6a (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You'll have to account for where every penny goes.[/ex]
	—unaccounted for [p]adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]3 [p]infml[/p] убивать (кого-л.); сбивать (что-л.); ловить (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[Т1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ The gunmen accounted for five terrorists at the airport.
	After a long hunt, the fox was at last accounted for.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 отдавать денежную компенсацию (за причинённый вред); отвечать по закону (за совершённое преступление):[/trn]
	\[Т1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ It will take him twenty years in prison to account for such a terrible crime.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 [b]account for preferences/tastes[/b] находить объяснение чьим-л. симпатиям и антипатиям:[/trn]
	\[(usu. neg.)\] [ex]♦ Have you seen the man she married?
	It shows that there's no accounting for tastes![/ex]
	
