bring out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 вытаскивать, вынимать (откуда-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]X9 + OUT (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Suddenly the man brought out a gun and threatened the driver with it. As I brought the handkerchief out of my pocket, several other objects fell out with it. [/ex]
	→ pull out (1)
	[m1][trn]2 выносить (что-л.) или выводить (кого-л.) на улицу, на свежий воздух:[/trn]
	\[T1 + OUT\] [ex]♦ It's warm enough to bring out the garden chairs. Why don't you bring the children out here in the sun?[/ex]
	→ fetch out (1)
	[m1][trn]3 выставлять на обозрение; выпускать; распускаться:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Jane never brings out her best dishes even when guests arrive. The warm sun brought the flowers out.[/ex] → be out (5), come out (5), fetch out (2)
	[m1][trn]4 also show up выявлять, обнаруживать:[/trn]
	\[T1 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Difficulties can bring out a person's best qualities. The new dress brought out her hidden beauty. The teacher helped to bring out the meaning of the poem. Plenty of money often brings out the worst in someone.[/ex] 
	—well-brought-out [p] adj[/p] → call forth, call out (3), come out (7), draw forth, draw out (8), fetch out (3)
	[m1][trn]5 производить, выпускать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Tom has brought out another new book. The makers are bringing out a new kind of soap.[/ex]
	→ be out (21), come out (8), fetch out (4), get out (13)
	[m1][trn]6 поощрять (кого-л.) высказаться, преодолеть застенчивость и т. п., особ. в выражении: [b]bring someone out of his shell[/b]:[/trn]
	\[T1 (of) \] [ex]♦ Mary is very quiet, try to bring her out (of her shelf) at the party.[/ex] → come out of (4), draw out (9), fetch out (5), lead out (2)
	[m1][trn]7 устроить, вызвать забастовку:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We'll bring the workers out for more pay.[/ex] → be out (13), call out (4), come out (15), fetch out (6), get out (17), go back (8), go out (13), lay down (13), put down (18), stay out (3), stop out (2), walk out (3)
	[m1][trn]8 [p] BrE becoming rare[/p] вывозить (обыч. молодую девушку) в свет:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Is Mrs King- Brown bringing her daughter out this year? [/ex]
	→ come out (16)
	[m1][trn]9 сделать вызов, приглашение (кому-л.) в какую-л. страну:[/trn]
