	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ The politician's closing words brought the whole crowd to their feet, cheering wildly.[/ex] → get to (11), etc.
	[m1][trn]10 [b]bring someone to the fore[/b] выдвинуть кого-л. в передние ряды, в руководители и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Не had never been anything more than a good official, but wartime conditions brought him quickly to the fore because of the special qualities of his character.[/ex]
	→ come to2 (22)
	[m1][trn]11 [b]bring someone to grips with[/b] something заставить кого-л. заняться проблемой и т. п. вплотную:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ There was по escape from the facts; we were brought to grips with the hard reality of our position.[/ex]
	→ come to2 (24), get to (13)
	[m1][trn]12 [b]bring something to the ground[/b] полностью разрушить, уничтожить:[/trn]
