	[m1][trn]13 [b]bring matters/things to a head[/b] вызывать обострение проблемы для скорейшего сё разрешения; доводить дело до критической точки:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Matters have been brought to a head in the peace talks; tomorrow they will either succeed or fail. [/ex]→ come to2 (26)
	[m1][trn]14 [b]bring someone to heel[/b] [p]not fml[/p] заставить кого-л. подчиниться:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Someone who refuses to follow the party line must be brought to heel before he does lasting damage.[/ex] → come to2 (27)
	[m1][trn]15[b] bring someone to himself[/b] привести кого-л. в сознание, вернуть кого-л. к действительности:[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Some cold water on her face might bring her to herself. The sudden sound of the train whistle brought me to myself; I had not known how far I had been walking, deep in thought.[/ex] → come to2 (32)
	[m1][trn]16 [b]bring someone to his knees[/b] одержать полную победу над кем-л., победить кого-л.:[/trn]
