brood over
brood upon
	[p] v prep[/p]
	→ think about (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]предаваться размышлениям (часто бесполезным):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + about/on/over/upon[/com]\] [ex]♦ It's no good brooding about your troubles. Sandra has been brooding over that boy for too long. Why brood on how it happened? The thing to do is put it right.[/ex]
	
browbeat into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]выбивать (что-л.) угрозами:[/trn]
	\[V4b\] [ex]♦ We shall never allow our police to browbeat prisoners into admitting their guilt.[/ex]
	
brown off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ cheese off, feed up (2), tire of (2)[p] 
	[m1][trn]infml[/p] утомлять; наскучивать, нагонять скуку, тоску:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Why should you feel browned off? You're supposed to be on holiday. All this endless bad news browns me off.[/ex]
	
browse among
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	→ browse through.
	
browse on
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn][i](о животном)[/i] объедать, ощипывать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Many animals like to browse on leaves.[/ex]
	
browse through
browse among
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]просматривать, проглядывать, листать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + through/among (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I can spend hours just browsing through books in the library.[/ex]
	
bruit abroad
bruit about
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ blaze abroad, noise abroad, rumour abroad, spread abroad
	[p] fml or pomp[/p]
	[m1][trn]стать широко известным, прославиться:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The representative's job is to bruit the company's products abroad.[/ex]
	
brush aside
brush away
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 смахивать:[/trn]
	\[X9 + ASIDE AWAY\] [ex]♦ Mother was in the garage, brushing the dirt aside. Brushing away her tears she promised to return.[/ex]
	→ sweep aside (1)
	[m1][trn]2 отметать с лёгкостью, отделываться:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Brushing the enemy aside, we swept into the next town.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 игнорировать, не замечать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Brushing away all opposition, he put the matter to a vote. You can't brush your difficulties aside in that easy manner.[/ex]
	→ sweep aside (2)
	
brush down
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 сметать (пыль), счищать (грязь):[/trn]
	\[T1 + DOWN) [ex]♦ Come and help me to brush the horses down. She picked herself up, brushed herself down, and started walking again.[/ex] 
	— brush-down [p]n[/p]
	→ dust down (1)
	[m1][trn]2 отчитывать, делать выговор:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (for) [/com]\] [ex]♦ I could hear the director brushing Jim down for being late again.[/ex] 
	— brushing-down [p]n[/p]
	→ tell off (1), etc.
	
brush off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 удалять(ся) или счищать(ся) щёткой:[/trn]
	\[L9 + OFF\] [ex]♦ Don't worry about that mark, it will brush off.[/ex]
	\[X9 + OFF) [ex]♦ Please brush this insect off[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]infml[/p] отделываться, отмахиваться от (чего-л.); давать отставку (кому-л.), отшивать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (simple tenses)/] [ex]♦ The committee brushed off his enquiries with meaningless promises. Jim's girlfriend brushed him off before he met Mary.[/ex] —brush-off [p]n[/p]
	
brush over
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 подметать (пол):[/trn]
	\[T1 + OVER\] [ex]♦ Please brush the floor over when you have finished.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 коснуться (чего-л.) вскользь:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1a (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The chairman brushed over the question of your appointment.[/ex]
	
brush past
	[p]v adv; prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]проскользнуть, прошмыгнуть мимо (чего-л. или кого-л.); слегка задеть (кого-л.), проходя мимо:[/trn]
	\[L9 + PAST/pasf\] [ex]♦ There was only just room to brush past (the pillar) in the crowd.[/ex]
	
brush up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 зачёсывать вверх:[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP\] [ex]♦ Don't brush my hair up the wrong way, it hurts.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]not fml[/p] освежить в памяти; повторить выученное; усовершенствовать свои знания:[/trn]
	\[Tia\][ex]♦ I must brush up my French before I go to Paris.[/ex] → polish up (2), rub up (2)
	
brush up against
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 слегка дотронуться (до чего-л.), легко коснуться (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[L9 + UP + against\] [ex]♦ I brushed up against the door, and some of the wet paint came off onto my coat.[/ex] → rub against, rub up against (1)
	[m1][trn]2 неожиданно натолкнуться:[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ I hadn't thought that we would brush up against so much opposition in this town.[/ex] → rub up against (2)
	
bubble over
	[p]v adv[/p] 
	→ brim over
	[m1][trn]1переливаться через край:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Look out! The pan of milk is bubbling over![/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 переполняться (чувствами):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (into)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Her nervousness bubbled over into foolish laughter. [/ex]
	
bubble over with
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p] 
	→ brim over with 
	переполняться (чувствами); бить ключом [i](об эмоциях):[/i]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Mary was bubbling over with joy.[/ex]
	
buck off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn][i] (о лошади) [/i]сбрасывать седока:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Some horses are specialy trained to buck their riders off, to amuse the crowd at an outdoor performance.[/ex]
	
buck up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p]BrE infml[/p] спешить, торопиться:[/trn]
	\[IØ (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Buck up, we're all waiting. [/ex]→ bustle up, hurry up (1)
	[m1][trn]2 [p]infml[/p] стараться улучшить, усовершенетвовать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You'd better buck up your ideas.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [p]infml[/p] подбодрить(ся), встряхнуть(ся):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ A good holiday will buck you up.[/ex]
	\[IØ (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Buck up, your troubles will soon be over.[/ex] → cheer up, etc.
	
buckle down
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ buckle to, knuckle down (2)[p] 
	[m1][trn]not fml[/p] начать серьёзно работать (над чем-л.); всерьёз взяться (за что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (to) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ It's time you buckled down and got some work done. It's time you buckled down to some work.[/ex]
	
buckle to
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ buckle down, knuckle down (2)[p] 
	[m1][trn]not fml[/p] энергично приниматься всем вместе за дело:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ If we all buckle to, we'll soon get the job done.[/ex]
	
buckle under
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ knuckle under 
	[m1][trn]признать своё поражение; уступать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (to) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ In the end he had to buckle under and admit that he was wrong. We all had to buckle under to the director's orders.[/ex]
	
buckle up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 скреплять пряжкой, застёгивать на пряжку:[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP\] [ex]♦ Wendy can already buckle up her shoes although she's only six.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 гнуться, выгибаться; коробиться:[/trn]
	\[IØ + UP\] [ex]♦ Because it was so hot, the metal bridge buckled up, and the cars which were crossing it fell into the river.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [p]not fml[/p] застёгиваться ремнём безопасности в автомобиле:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ According to the new law, all drivers and passengers must buckle up.[/ex]
	→ belt up (4), strap in
	
budget for
	[p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]ассигновать достаточно денег на (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The university had to budget for an increase in the number of students.[/ex]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ We shall have to budget an additional amount for the new baby's needs.[/ex]
	
bug out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn][p] AmE mil infml[/p] спешно собраться и перебраться в другое место:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Is it true the whole camp is going to bug out in the morning, captain?[/ex] 
	—bug-out [p]n[/p]
	
bugger about
bugger around
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p] taboo sl[/p] бездельничать, слоняться без дела:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Stop buggering about and get on with some work.[/ex]
	→ mess about (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 [p] taboo sl[/p] создавать трудности для (кого-л.), мешать (кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1b\] [ex]♦ Leave те alone and stop buggering me about.[/ex]
	→ mess about (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 [p] taboo sl[/p] разбрасывать (что-л.); приводить в беспорядок:[/trn]
	\[T1b\] [ex]♦ Who's been buggering my papers about? I left them all tidy, and now here they are all over the floor.[/ex] mess about (3). etc.
	
bugger about with
bugger around with
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[p]v prep[/p]
	→ mess about with (1), etc.[p] 
	[m1][trn]taboo sl[/p] приводить в беспорядок; рыться (в чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I'm sure somebody's been buggering about with my record player.[/ex]
	
bugger off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ push off (3), etc. 
	[m1][trn][p] taboo sl[/p] уйти, убираться прочь:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (simple tenses, usu. imper.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Bugger off, will you? I don't want you here.[/ex]
	
bugger up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ mess up (2), etc.[p] 
	[m1][trn]taboo sl[/p] испортить, загубить, напортачить:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ If John buggers up his driving test again, I doubt if he'll ever pass it.[/ex]
	
build in
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 встраивать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ These cupboards have been built in.[/ex] 
	—built-in [p]adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]2 быть составной частью (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The difficulties seem to be built in. [/ex]
	—built-in [p]adj[/p]
	
build into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 сооружать, создавать (что-л. из чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + into\] Не took some nails and bits of wood, and built them into a rough cupboard.
	\[[com][/ex]IØ + into[/com]\] [ex]♦ These native pots are slowly building into a fine collection.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 встраивать, вделывать (во что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ These cupboards are built into the walls.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 сделать составной частью (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The difficulties are built into the work. The rate of pay was built into her contract.[/ex]
	
build on
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]пристраивать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ This part of the hospital was built on later.[/ex]
	
build on
build upon
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 строить на (чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + on/upon[/com]\] [ex]♦ We built the house on our own land.[/ex] 
	— unbuilt-on [p]adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]2 рассчитывать на (что-л.); полагаться на (кого-л. или что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I'd like to come with you but that's not a promise, don't build on it.[/ex]
	\[T4\] [ex]♦ Don't build on going abroad this summer, we may not have enough money.[/ex]
	→ depend on (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 основывать (что-л. на чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Don't build your hopes on the chairman's promises. The insurance business is built on trust.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 лежать в основе (чего-л.), полагаться на (что-л.) в дальнейшем развитии:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ 1п her new job she'll be able to build on her previous experience in marketing.[/ex]
	
build of
build out of
	[p] v (adv) prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]выделывать (что-л. из какого-л. материала); изготовлять:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (+ OUT) + of[/com]\] [ex]♦ Before bricks were invented, people built their houses out of wood.[/ex]
	
build over
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ build up (5) 
	[m1][trn]застраивать (участок) зданиями:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The fields where I played as a child have been built over.[/ex] 
	—built-over [p]adj[/p]
	
build up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 наращивать, увеличивать:[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP\] [ex]♦ Use more bricks to build the wall up.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 накапливать(ся), сосредоточивать(ся), наращивать(ся); укреплять(ся):[/trn]
	\[IØ (into, to)\] [ex]♦ The clouds are building up. Enemy forces have now built up to a dangerous strength. Our hopes for peace are building up.[/ex]
	\[[com]T1 (from, into,[/ex] to)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You must build up your strength after your illness. He has built up a good business over the years from a small beginning.[/ex]
	—buildup [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]3 [i] (о деньгах)[/i] накоплять(ся); сколачивать капитал:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Му savings are building up nicely.[/ex]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ You can build up a fortune by regularly saving money.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [i] (о транепорте)[/i] создавать пробки:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ A long line of vehicles has built up by the narrow bridge.[/ex] 
	—buildup [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]5 застраивать (участок) зданиями; возводить здания (где-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu.[/ex] pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The area has been built up since I lived here. [/ex]
	—built-up [p]adj[/p]
	→ build over
	[m1][trn]6 [p]not fml[/p] разрекламировать (кого-л. или что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The singer has been built up into a great success.[/ex] 
	—buildup [p]n[/p]
	
bulge out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]выдаваться, выпячиваться:[/trn]
	\[IØ + OUT) [ex]♦ The boy put so many things into his pocket that it bulged out.[/ex]
	
bulk large
	[p]v adj[/p]
	→ loom large[p] 
	[m1][trn]not fml[/p] быть или казаться важным:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The question of replacing the director bulks large with the committee.[/ex]
	
bulk up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn][p]not fml[/p] увеличиваться, расти; составлять сумму:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (to) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Your money could bulk up to a fortune if you save everything you can.[/ex]
	
bully into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]силой или угрозами заставить (делать что-л.), запугивать:[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Those boys will have to be bullied into action.[/ex]
	\[V4b\] [ex]♦ The boys bullied the small girl into giving them all her money.[/ex]
	
bully off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ face off
	[m1][trn]начинать игру в хоккей на траве:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Аге you ready to bully off?[/ex] 
	—bully-off [p]n[/p]
	
bum about
bum around
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn][p] sl[/p] бездельничать, лоботрясничать, слоняться без дела:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I've been bumming around for the last year without a job.[/ex]
	
bum along
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p] sl[/p] ровно ехать (в автомобиле):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ We were just bumming along nicely when the tyre burst.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p] sl[/p] успешно продвигаться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How's your work going? Oh, just bumming along, thanks.[/ex]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn][p] sl[/p] ровно ехать (в автомобиле):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We were just bumming along the road when the tire burst.[/ex]
	
bumble through
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]вести беспорядочную жизнь, кое-как справляться со своими делами:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Mr Green just bumbles through life, I don't know how he ever gets anything done.[/ex]
	
bump into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 наталкиваться, налетать на (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I've bumped into the door again and hurt my knee.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]infml[/p] случайно встретить (кого-л), натолкнуться на (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I bumped into an old friend in town today.[/ex]
	→ bang into (2), barge into (4), knock into (2), knock up against (2), run into (7)
	
bump off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ do away with (2), do for (7), do in (1), finish off (4), knock off (5), look after (3), make away with (2), polish off (3), rub out (2)[p] 
	[m1][trn]sl[/p] убить, убрать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The old man who owned the jewels was bumped off by the thieves.[/ex]
	
bump up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p]infml[/p] увеличивать, поднимать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Two more good results will bump up your average.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [b]be bumped up[/b] [p]infml[/p] получать повышение по службе (часто незаслуженно):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ I don't like the new director much, he seems to have been bumped up from some more humble position [/ex]
	—bumped-up [p]adj[/p] → jump up (3)
	
bunch up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]собирать в пучки; сбиваться в кучу:[/trn]
	\[Т1 + UP\] [ex]♦ Don't bunch the flowers up so tightly, you'll spoil them.[/ex]
	\[[com]IØ + UP (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The singers bunched up to make room for one more.[/ex]
	
bundle away
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ bundle off (2), pack off (2)
	[m1][trn]спешно спроваживать; поспешно уходить; покидать в спешке:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The children were bundled away when the guests arrived.[/ex]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The women bundled away when their husbands returned.[/ex]
	
bundle into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 усаживать (кого-л. в автомобиль и т. п ):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The guest got very drunk so they bundled him into a taxi and sent him home.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 запихивать, засовывать:[/trn]
	\[D1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Don't bundle all the clothes into that bag so carelessly.[/ex]

bundle off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отсылать:[/trn]
	\[T1 + OFF\] [ex]♦ Could you bundle these clothes off to my sister?[/ex]
	→ pack off (1)
	[m1][trn]2 спешно спроваживать; поспешно уходить; покидать в спешке:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ The women bundled off when their husbands arrived.[/ex]
	\[T1 [i](usu. pass.)[/i]\] The children were bundled off to bed as soon as the guests arrived.[/ex] → bundle away, pack off (2)
	[m1][trn]3 спешно отсылать (кого-л.), спроваживать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (to) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The family were so ashamed of the youngest son that they bundled him off to Canada.[/ex]
	→ pack off (3)
	
bundle out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]поспешно выходить (из автомобиля и т. п.); выпроваживать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ The taxi door burst open and all the children bundled out.[/ex]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I shall bundle you out of here very fast if you don't leave by yourself.[/ex]
	
bundle up
	[p]v adv[/p]
