	[m1][trn]1 вернуть(ся) мысленно назад; вспоминать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Let us cast back our minds to the first meeting.[/ex]
	\[IØ (in) (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ let us cast back in our minds to the first meeting.[/ex] → throw back (6)
	[m1][trn]2 [p]AmE[/p] походить на своего дальнего предка:[/trn]
	\[IØ (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ The boy casts back to his great-great-grandfather.[/ex] → throw back (5)
	
cast before
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn][b]cast pearls before swine[/b] метать бисер перед свиньями; зря терять время с кем-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Не tried to explain the beauty of the music to his pupils but it was just casting pearls before swine.[/ex]
	
cast down
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 указывать на (что-л. внизу):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + DOWN (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The girl cast her eyes down modestly,[/ex] 
	—downcast [p]adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]2 разрушать (что-л.); разбивать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + DOWN) [ex]♦ True believers must cast down the temples of the false gods.[/ex] → throw down1 (3)
	[m1][trn]3 повергать в уныние:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Mary was cast down by the bad news about her mother.[/ex] 
	—downcast [p]adj[/p]
	
cast in
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 давать роль в пьесе (кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + in\] [ex]♦ The director has cast you and Mary in the parts of the sisters.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 выражать (свои мысли в определённой форме):[/trn]
	\[D1 \] [ex]♦ Не tends to cast his ideas in long sentences.[/ex] recast in
	[m1][trn]3 [b]be cast in the same/a different mould[/b] [p]not fml[/p] быть такого же/другого склада:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ You can't expect the same behaviour from John as from his sister; he's cast in a different mould. The brothers think exactly alike, as if they were cast in the same mould.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [b]cast in someone's face/teeth[/b] [p]not fml[/p] упрекать, обвинять кого-л. (в чём-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ There's no need to cast his recent failure in his teeth in that unkind way.[/ex]
	→ fling in2 (2), throw in2 (3)
	
cast in with
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p] 
	→ fling in with, throw in with
	[m1][trn][b]cast in one's lot with[/b] связаться с (кем-л. или какой-л. политической партией), присоединиться (к кому-л. или к какой-л. политической партии):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I'm sorry that the boy has cast in his lot with such undesirable people.[/ex]
	
cast off
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 сбрасывать, скидывать:[/trn]
	\[X9 + OFF\] [ex]♦ As the sun grew warmer, he cast off his heavy winter clothes.[/ex] → cast aside (1), fling aside (1), fling off (1), lay off (8), leave off (1), shake off1 (1), throw aside (1), throw off1 (1, 2), toss aside (1), toss off (1)
	[m1][trn]2 выкидывать за ненадобностью; удалять:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ When you grow too big for your clothes, cast them off and I'll give them away,[/ex] 
	—castoff [p]n[/p] 
	—cast-off [p] adj[/p] 
	—offcast [p] n, adj AmE[/p]
	[m1][trn]3 бросать, покидать, рвать отношения:[/trn]
	\[Т1 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ When he grew rich, he cast off his old friends,[/ex] 
	-cast-off [p]adj[/p] → cast aside (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 скидывать, сбрасывать, освобождаться:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ He was pleased to be able to cast off such an unwelcome responsibility. The Russian people rose, casting off the chains of unjust rule.[/ex] 
	—offcast [p]adj[/p] → fling off (3), etc.
	[m1][trn]5 сбрасывать (кожу и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The snake cast off its old skin.[/ex] → shuffle off (2), slough off (1)
	[m1][trn]6 отдавать швартовы; отваливать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Don't cast off the boat till everyone is on board. Cast off all ropes![/ex]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Are you ready to cast off?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 esp. [p] BrE[/p] [i](в вязанье)[/i] спускать петли:[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ At the end of the row, cast off seven stitches.[/ex]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Be careful not to cast off too tightly, or the work will lose its shape. [/ex]→ bind off, cast on1
	[m1][trn]8 [i](в полиграфии)[/i] определять по рукописи объём печатной работы:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I've cast off your book and think it should come to about 400 pages when it's printed,[/ex] 
	—cast off [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]9 [i](в деревенеком танце)[/i] оставить своего партнёра и пройти круг до конца:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ After the next figure, you cast off and meet your partner again at the other end.[/ex]
	
cast on
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ bind off, cast off (7)[i] 
	[m1][trn](в вязанье)[/i] набирать (первые петли):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Cast on seventy-six stitches and work two inches of plain stitch.[/ex]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ I'll start cooking the dinner as soon as I've finished casting on.[/ex]
	
cast on
cast upon
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 бросать на (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]X9 + on/upon (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The storm cast the little boat on the rocks. The traveller cast his money on the table and left.[/ex]
	→ fling on2 (1), throw on2 (1)
	[m1][trn]2 [b]cast one's bread on the waters[/b] отпускай хлеб свой по водам (Диблия); делай добро, и оно может вернуться к тебе:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ "Cast thy bread upon the waters; for thou shalt find it after many days.[/ex]" (The Bible)
	[m1][trn]3 [b]cast doubt on[/b] заронять сомнение в правдивости (чего-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Everyone was prepared to accept the prisoner's story until the opposing lawyer cast doubt on it.[/ex] → throw on2 (6)
	[m1][trn]4 [b]cast oneself on someone's mercy[/b] отдаться на милость кого-л.:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ If the judge finds you guilty, you can only cast yourself on his mercy.[/ex] → fling on2 (2), throw on2 (8)
	[m1][trn]5 [b]cast one's/а shadow on[/b] отбрасывать тень на (что-л.); заслонять от света:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ After dinner, the office block to the west casts its shadow on our windows, so we don't see the setting sun. [/ex]→ cast over (3), throw on2 (2), throw over2 (3)
	
cast out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отбрасывать, откидывать; выкидывать:[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 + out (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I really must cast out all these old papers. Perfect love casts out fear. The magician claims to be able to cast out devils.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 изгонять из общества; заставить уйти:[/trn] 
	\[[com]Т1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ In former times, criminals were often cast out and had to live in the wild. [/ex]
	—outcast [p]n[/p] → throw out (4), etc.
	
cast over
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]закрывать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Her eyes were cast over with sorrow.[/ex] 
	—overcast [p]adj[/p]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [b]cast a damper over[/b] [p]not fml[/p] расхолаживать; убавлять веселья:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Mary's absence cast a damper over the party.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [b]cast an/one's eye over[/b] пробегать глазами; быстро просмотреть:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ I'd like you to cast your eyes over this letter before I send it to the school, to see if it's satisfactory.[/ex]
	→ pass over2 (4)
	[m1][trn]3 [b]cast а/one's shadow over[/b] отбрасывать тень на (что-л.); заслонять от света:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Please stand to one side, you're casting your shadow over my work.[/ex]
	→ cast on2 (5), throw on2 (2), throw over2 (3)
	
cast up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 выбрасывать вверх, выкидывать, извергать:[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP\] [ex]♦ The machine cast up great heaps of earth.[/ex] chuck up (1), fling up (1), throw up (1), toss up (1)
	[m1][trn]2 выбрасывать на берег:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (on) (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Pieces of wood are cast up all along this coast. A body was cast up last night.[/ex]
	→ wash up (3)
	[m1][trn]3 подсчитать; суммировать; подводить итог:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Please cast up this list of figures for me.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 напоминать (кому-л. о чём-л. неприятном); припоминать (недостатки и т. п ):[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 (at) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Не is always casting up my old failures (at me).[/ex]
	→ fling up (6), sling up (2), throw up (7)
	[m1][trn]5 esp. [p]AmE not fml[/p] рвать, тошнить:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Jane has cast up her dinner again.[/ex]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Jane has been casting up all morning.[/ex] → bring up (4), etc.
	
catch alight
