	[m1][trn]1 загораться, воспламеняться:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + alight (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Some dry leaves caught alight and soon the whole forest was on fire. [/ex]
	→ place to (3), put to2 (17), set alight (1), set on2 (10), set to2 (5)
	[m1][trn]2 зажечься (чувством), воспылать; стать очень привлекательным:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ At the end of his speech, the crowd caught alight and began cheering wildly.[/ex]
	→ set alight (2)
	
catch at
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 поймать, застигнуть (кого-л.); захватить с поличным:[/trn]
	\[T1 + at (usu. simple tenses)\] I've caught you at your tricks again.[/ex] → grab at (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 ухватиться (за какую-л. возможность и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ A business man will catch at any chance of making a profit.[/ex] → clutch at (2), grab at (2), snap at (3), snatch at (2)
	[m1][trn]3 catch at a straw хвататься за соломинку:[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ "A drowning man will catch at a straw."[/ex] (saying) → grab at (3), etc.
	
