	\[Х9 + IN (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ You might catch him in about 11 o'clock.[/ex] → catch out (1)
	[m1][trn]2 ушить, прихватить, затянуть:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Catch in the waistline very lightly so that it doesn't show.[/ex] → catch up (6)
	
catch in
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 зацепиться за (что-л.); споткнуться о (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + in (often simple tenses) [ex]♦ "I left the room... but caught my foot in the meat." [/ex](George and Weedon Grossmith, [i]The Diary of a Nobody)[/i]
	\[[com]IØ + in (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ My foot caught in the mat and I fell heavily.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [b]catch someone in the act[/b] застать кого-л. на месте преступления, захватить кого-л.с поличным:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The policeman followed the thieves until they actually picked up the jewels, when he caught them in the act.[/ex] → <<catch redhanded>>.
	
catch it
	v pron
	[m1][trn][p]infml[/p] получить нагоняй:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ You'll catch it when your mother learns who broke the dishes.[/ex]
	
catch napping
	[p]v adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 застать (кого-л.) спящим:[/trn]
	\[X9 + napping! [ex]♦ Father was supposed to be working, but when I went in I caught him napping.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]infml[/p] поймать (кого-л.) на ошибке, застигнуть врасплох:[/trn]
	\[T1b\] [ex]♦ There's another mistake on page thirty-two, I'm afraid I've caught you napping again![/ex]
	
catch of
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [b]catch hold of[/b]:[/trn]
	[m1][trn]а ухватить (что-л. или кого-л.), ухватиться (за что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Catching hold of the rope, the climber was able to swing to safety.[/ex]
	→ get of (7)
	[m1][trn]b начать понимать, схватывать (мысль):[/trn]
