	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]раскрашивать (рисунок):[/trn]
	\[T1 + IN\] [ex]♦ The child coloured in the picture.[/ex]
	
colour up
color up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 покраснеть (от стыда, смущения):[/trn]
	\[L9 + UP\] [ex]♦ Mary coloured up when Jim praised her cooking.[/ex]
	→ flame up (3), flush up
	[m1][trn]2 приукрашивать (рассказ и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The sailor always colours up his adventures to please his hearers.[/ex]
	
comb for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]прочёсывать (местность и т. п.) в поисках (чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + for[/com]\] [ex]♦ The police are combing the woods for the missing boy. I've combed the house for your bag, but it's not here.[/ex]
	
comb out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 расчёсывать (волосы):[/trn]
	\[X9 + OUT\] [ex]♦ She spent hours in front of the mirror, combing out her long hair.[/ex] → comb through (1)
	[m1][trn]2 удалять (что-л.) из волос, вычёсывать, расчёсывать:[/trn] 
	\[Х9 + OUT\] [ex]♦ She had to spend hours combing out the knots every time she washed her hair. When the weather turns hot we help the dog to keep cool by combing out his loose hairs.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 прочёсывать (местность и т. п.) в поисках (чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + OUT\] [ex]♦ The villagers combed out the woods, looking for the missing boy.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 искать (что-л. где-л.), выискивать (что-л. где-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The student spent many hours in the library, combing out the facts she wanted in the old books.[/ex]
	→ comb through (2)
	[m1][trn]5 [p]not fml[/p] выгонять (что-л. или кого-л.), исключать (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The committee's job is to comb out those students who are not likely to succeed.[/ex]
	→ weed out [b](2)[/b]

comb through
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 тщательно расчёсывать (волосы):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + through[/com]\] [ex]♦ She spent hours in front of the mirror, combing through her long hair.[/ex]
	→ comb out (1)
	[m1][trn]2 усиленно искать (где-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The student spent many hours in the library combing through old books looking for the facts that she wanted.[/ex]
	→ comb out (4)
	
combine against
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]объединять силы, чтобы противостоять (чему-л. или кому-л.), объединяться против (чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + against[/com]\] [ex]♦ Let us combine our two firms against our competitors.[/ex]
	
combine with
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 соединять(ся) (с чем-л.), объединять(ся):[/trn]
	\[[com]X9 + with[/com]\] [ex]♦ The members decided to combine the tennis club with the cricket club, forming one sports club.[/ex]
	\[[com]L9 + wtih (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ This chemical combines with air to form a liquid.[/ex]
	→ amalgamate with, merge together, merge with
	[m1][trn]2 добавлять (что-л. к чему-л.), присоединять (что-л. к чему-л. ):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ When rising prices are combined with a lack of jobs, many people suffer and the nation becomes poorer. If he can combine his natural ability with hard work, he should be very successful.[/ex]
	
come aboard
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ go aboard, go ashore, take aboard, take ashore, take on (1)
	[m1][trn]садиться на корабль или самолёт:[/trn]
	\[L9 + ABOARD\] [ex]♦ "When does the pilot come aboard?" "Just before we enter the harbour." Come aboard! You're all welcome here![/ex]
	
come about
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 происходить, случаться, возникать:[/trn]
	\[IØ (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Peace can only come about if each side agrees to yield to the other. 
	\[It + L9\] [ex]♦ "It all came about in a way which is worth recalling, if only for the light it throws on our Captain's character."[/ex] (Laurens van der Post, [ex]♦ The Hunter and the Whale)[/ex]
	\[[com]It + I5 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How did it come about that the man was dismissed?[/ex]
	→ bring about (1)
	[m1][trn]2 [i](о судне или ветре)[/i] менять направление на противоположное:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ It was too stormy to continue the voyage, so the ship came about and headed for the safety of the shore.[/ex]
	→ bring about (2), etc.
	
come across
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 проходить небольшое расстояние, пересекать, переходить через дорогу и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[IØ + ACROSS\] [ex]♦ When the traffic has all passed, it's safe to come across. Why don't you come across to our house this evening? Many more people have come across to the island since the new bridge was built.[/ex] → come over1 (3), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 быть понятным, доходить до сознания:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Did his speech come across?[/ex]
	→ come over1 (4), get across1 (2), get over1 (3), get through1 (7), get through to (2), go across1 (2), go down (15), go down with (2), go over1 (4), put across1 (2), put over2 (2)
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 пересекать (комнату и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[IØ + across\] [ex]♦The host came across the room to greet his guests.[/ex] → go across2, etc.
	[m1][trn]2 случайно найти (что-л.) или встретить (кого-л.), натолкнуться (на что-л. или кого-л. ):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass., simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ I came across this old photograph in the back of the drawer. Outside the restaurant, we came across a man doing a fire-eating performance. [/ex]→ happen on, etc.
	[m1][trn]3 прийти (в голову), появиться (в мыслях):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass., simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ The thought came across my mind that I had met him before.
	\[[com]It + T5 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ It came across my mind that I had met him before.[/ex]
	
come across as
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn][p]infml[/p] казаться (кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[1,1\] [ex]♦ He comes across as someone who means what he says.
	\[[/ex]L4\] [ex]♦ He comes across as being very sincere.[/ex]
	
come across with
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 плыть по морю вместе (с кем-л.), отправляться в путь вместе (с кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + ACROSS + with[/com]\] [ex]♦ Му grandfather came across with the first party of settlers.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 → COME THROUGH WITH[/trn]
	
come after
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 следовать (за чем-л. или кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + after (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I can never remember which king came after which.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 преследовать (обыкн. кого-л.) с целью нападения:[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass.)\] [ex]♦ I saw the big dog coming after me.[/ex] 
	→ be after (2), come at (3), come for (2), get after (1), go after (1), go at (3), go for (4), keep after (1), make after, make at (2), make for (3)
	
come again
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 приходить ещё; возвращаться:[/trn]
	\[IØ + again\] [ex]♦ I'm so glad you enjoyed your visit; do come again.[/ex]
	→ go back (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 [p]BrE infml[/p] повторять сказанное:[/trn]
	\[IØ (simple tenses, usu. imper.)\] [ex]♦ Come again? I didn't hear what you said.[/ex] → come back (6)
	
come along
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 проходить, проезжать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + ALONG (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Just then a bus came along so we got on and rode home. My teacher came along iust as we were talking about him.[/ex]
	→ come by1 (1). get by1 (1), get past1 (1), go by1 (1), go past1 (1)
	[m1][trn]2 приходить, приезжать вместе с кем-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + ALONG (to) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Only Jane was invited to the party, but both her sisters came along too. [/ex]
	→ be along, bring along (1), get along (2), go along (2), send along, take along
	[m1][trn]3 случаться, происходить, появляться:[/trn]
	\[IØ (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Trouble comes along when you least expect it. Take every chance that comes along.[/ex] → turn up (10)
	[m1][trn]4 also come on идти [i](о делах),[/i] делать успехи, преуспевать:[/trn] 
	\[[com]IØ (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How is your work coming along? It's coming along nicely, thank you.[/ex]
	→ bring on (3), etc.
	[m1][trn]5 also come on поправлять здоровье, поправляться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The doctor says Mother is coming along nicely now, thank you.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 спешить, торопиться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (with) (usu. imper.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Come along, children, or we'll be late! [/ex]
	→ come on1 (8) 
	[m1][trn]7 also come on прилагать больше усилий, работать усерднее;[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. imper.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Come along, Jane, you can do better than that.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 [p]infml[/p] я тебе не верю!, быть не может![/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (imper.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Oh, come along! I know better than that![/ex]
	→ come on1 (10), etc.
	
come amiss
