	\[[com]IØ (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I hope nothing comes amiss when we move into our new house.[/ex]
	
come apart
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 разваливаться, рассыпаться па куски:[/trn]
	\[IØ (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ It just came apart in my hands.[/ex] → fall apart (1), fall to2 (3)
	[m1][trn]2 [b]come apart at the seams[/b] [p]not fml[/p] разваливаться, лопнуть по швам, расклеиться:[/trn] 
	\[often continuous tenses\] [ex]♦ Their clever plan came apart at the seams when the government changed the tax laws. I'm rather worried about my secretary, he's been coming apart at the seams recently.[/ex]
	
come around
come round
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 объехать, обойти кругом:[/trn]
	\[IØ + AROUND/ROUND) [ex]♦ The road was flooded, so we had to come round by the bridge.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 заходить ненадолго, заглянуть:[/trn]
	\[IØ (to)\] [ex]♦ Why don't you come around and see us one evening?[/ex] → bring over (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 [i] (о судне или ветре)[/i] менять направление:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Just then the wind came round so we had to reset the sails. Take the wheel, see if you can stop her from coming around.[/ex] → bring about (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 происходить регулярно:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Birthdays come around too quickly when one is older.[/ex]
	→ roll around (3)
	[m1][trn]5 приходить в себя:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ The girl fainted, but she came round when we threw drops of water on her face.[/ex] → bring to (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]6 менять своё мнение:[/trn]
	\[IØ (to) \] [ex]♦ Don't worry about the chairman, he'll soon come around (to our opinion).[/ex] → bring round (3), etc.
	[m1][trn]7 мириться (после ссоры); приходить снова в хорошее настроение:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Jim and Магу often argue, but it doesn't take them long to come around. Father was in a very bad temper this morning, but he had come around by evening.[/ex]
	→ come to1 (2)
	
come at
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 прибывать, появляться (в определённое время):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + at[/com]\] [ex]♦ Some of the guests came at [/ex]7 [ex]♦ o'clock, others at 7.30.[/ex]
	→ go at (1)
	[m1][trn]2 находить (что-л.), добираться (до чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Put the food where the cat can't come at it. I wanted to reply to your letter in detail, but I can't come at it anywhere.[/ex]
	→ get at (1)
	[m1][trn]3 преследовать (обыкн. кого-л.) с целью нападения:[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ I saw the big dog coming at me.[/ex]
	→ come after (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 добраться (до чего-л.), раскрыть (что-л.), обнаружить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ It is always difficult to come at the truth.[/ex] → get at (2)
	
come away
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отпустить что-л., убрать (напр., руку):[/trn] 
	\[[com]IØ + AWAY (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ When my hand came away, blood poured from the wound.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 отламываться, отходить, отскакивать:[/trn] 
	\[[com]IØ + AWAY (from) (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I tried to pick up the bucket, but the handle came away in my hand.[/ex]
	→ take off1 (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 уходить, уезжать:[/trn] 
	\[[com]IØ + AWAY (with) (often simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Come away with me on my next holiday. I had to come away before the end of the party. The young writer asked his teacher's wife to come away with him.[/ex]
	→ go away (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 [p] ScotE not fml[/p] входить (в помещение):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (imper.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Come away! The door's open![/ex]
	
come away with
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 уходить, уезжать (с кем-л. или чем-л.):[/trn] 
	\[IØ + AWAY + with (often simple tenses)\] Come away with me on my next holiday. [/ex]→ go away (1)
	[m1][trn]2 уходить, уезжать (откуда-л. с добрыми чувствами, воспоминаниями и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 (no pass., simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ We came away with such happy memories of the town that we are sure to go back.[/ex]
	→ bring away, go away with (4), send away with (1)
	
come back
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 возвращаться:[/trn] 
	\[IØ + BACK (to)\] [ex]♦ We'd like to come back next year. When Jane comes back, will you give her a message?[/ex] → go back (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 вернуться к прежнему состоянию, профессии и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Is the singer expected to come back?[/ex] 
	—come-back [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]3 снова стать модным или популярным:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Long skirts are expected to come back next year.[/ex]
	→ be back (2)
	[m1][trn]4 вспоминаться, всплывать в памяти:[/trn]
	\[IØ (to) \] [ex]♦ Her name will come back (to me) soon.[/ex]
	\[[com]It + IØ (to) [/com]\] [ex]♦ It came back to me where I had seen her before.[/ex]
	→ bring back (2), call up (5), come back to (2), summon up (2)
	[m1][trn]5 отвечать, обыкн. резко; обрушиваться (на кого-л.):[/trn] 
	\[IØ (at, with) (simple tenses) [ex]♦ "But you're just as guilty!" Jane came back. She always comes back at anyone who tries to be polite to her. I shall speak for twenty minutes and then you can come back at me with your questions,[/ex] 
	—come-back [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]6 [p]infml[/p] повторять сказанное:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I didn't hear you, could you come back? I will now ask the first speaker to come back.[/ex]
	→ come again (2)
	[m1][trn]7 [i](о прежних методах и т. п.)[/i] вернуться, восстановиться:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Some people are hoping that the old system of punishment by death will come back.[/ex] → bring back (4)
	
come back to
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 возвращаться (в какое-л. место или к кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + BACK + to[/com]\] [ex]♦ I always come back to the same town for a holiday as it's so nice. [/ex]
	→ go back (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 вспоминаться, всплывать в памяти:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The details of the story are coming back to me now, although it happened a long time ago.[/ex] 
	\[It + T1\] [ex]♦ It suddenly came back to me where we met.[/ex]
	→ bring back (2), call up (5), come back (4), summon up (2)
	[m1][trn]3 возвращаться (к теме беседы):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I think it's time to come back to the most important question: who is to pay for the new building?[/ex] → get back (3), get back to (2), go back (4), go back to (3)
	
come before
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 предшествовать:[/trn]
