come under
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 зайти подо (что-л.), спрятаться под (чем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + under[/com]\] [ex]♦ Come under this tree with me and we'll both keep dry.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 also be under идти под (заголовком), подходить под (рубрику):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass., simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Your suggestion comes under (the general heading of) reorganization. [/ex]→ belong under, bring under (1), come within (1), fall into (3), fall under (3), go under2 (2) 
	[m1][trn]3 контролироваться (чем-л. или кем-л.), чувствовать власть (чего-л. или кого-л.), подпадать под влияние (чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ This area comes under the powers of the local court. In his youth he came under the influence of Beethoven.[/ex]
	→ be under (3), fall beneath (2), fall under (2)
	[m1][trn]4 испытать (что-л.), подвергнуться (чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The town came under attack again last night.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 come under fire [p]not fml[/p] подвергнуться критике, нападкам:[/trn]
	\[[com] no pass., often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The Minister's speech against the government came under fire from other Members of Parliament. The Minister came under fire when he opposed the government.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 come under the hammer → GO UNDER2 (4)[/trn]
	[m1][trn]7 come under observation быть под наблюдением, попасть под наблюдение:[/trn]
	\[[com]no pass., usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The brothers came under observation as soon as they left the prison.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 come under review рассматриваться, проверяться:[/trn]
	\[[com]no pass., usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Your pay comes under review every year.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 come under starter's orders [i](об участниках скачек)[/i] получить сигнал к началу забега:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The riders have come under starter's orders, but there may be delay before the start, as the horses are restless.[/ex] → be under (13)
	
come unstuck
	[p]v adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отклеиваться, отваливаться:[/trn]
	\[L7 + unstuck\] [ex]♦ I didn't open your letter, the envelope came unstuck.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]not fml[/p] столкнуться с трудностями, потерпеть неудачу:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ All his grand plans for the future of the firm came unstuck when the price of oil went up so much.[/ex]
	
come up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]I вставать, подниматься; расти:[/trn]
	\[L9 + UP) [ex]♦ I like to get up early and watch the sun come up. The flowers should be coming up now it is spring.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 подниматься (по лестнице, над поверхностью воды и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[IØ + UP\] [ex]♦ Ask the doctor to come up. His head came up for the third time: it was our last chance to save him from drowning.[/ex]
	→ bring up (1), go up1 (1), send up1 (1), take up (3)
	[m1][trn]3 заходить, наносить визит:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ "Come up and see me some time."[/ex] (Mae West in [i]Diamond Lib[/i])
	[m1][trn]4 возникать, случаться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I'll let you know if anything comes up. A chance may come up soon. A light wind came up.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 подходить:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ While I was waiting for the bus, a man came up and started asking questions. I could hear footsteps coming up behind me. More soldiers are coming up soon to help in the battle.[/ex]
	→ bring up (8)
	[m1][trn]6 ожидаться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (nontinuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ A new type of young parent is coming up. There's a new film coming up next week. What's coming up on the television?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 поступать, появляться в свою очередь:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ His case comes up next week. The furniture we want to buy is coming up next week at the auction.[/ex] → have up (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]8 всплывать [i](в беседе),[/i] быть упомянутым:[/trn]
	\[IØ (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Your question came up at the meeting. His name never comes up in our conversation these days.[/ex] → bring up (3), raise with
	[m1][trn]9 [p]infml[/p] выпадать, быть выбранным:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ My number will never come up.[/ex]
	10 [p]not fml[/p] победить, выиграть: 
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Did your horse come up?[/ex]
