	\[Х9 + AWAY\] [ex]♦ If you cut away some of the dead wood, you will have a healthier tree. The doctor had to cut away some flesh from the wounded leg.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 срезать (часть чего-л.); давать в разрезе:[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + AWAY (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The front of the coat was cut away to show the colours underneath. The collar was cut away according to the fashion. The working model was cut away to show the inside of the building. [/ex]
	—cutaway [p]adj[/p]
	
cut back
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 подрезать, укорачивать (растения и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + BACK\] [ex]♦ Gardeners argue about whether one should cut roses back in the spring or autumn.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 смещать события, возвращаться к более ранним событиям:[/trn]
	\[L9 + BACK (tо)\] [ex]♦ The film cut back to the earlier scene so that we understood her reasons.[/ex] 
	—cut-back [p]n[/p] → flash back, flash forward
	[m1][trn]3 резко менять направление на бегу:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + BACK (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The footballer pretended to run forward, then cut back and took the ball the other way.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [p]not fml[/p] сокращать (что-л.), уменьшать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The factory's production has been cut back.[/ex]
	\[IØ (on)\] [ex]♦ We shall have to cut back on our spending,[/ex] 
	—cut-back [p]n[/p] → cut down (3), cut down on
	[m1][trn]5 сокращать (слово):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ This word has been cut back to save space.[/ex] 
	— cutback [p] n,[/p] 
	— cutback [p]adj[/p]
	
cut dead
	[p]v adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]делать вид, что не замечаешь (кого-л); притворяться, что не знаешь (кого-л.):[/trn] 
	\[Х7 + dead\] [ex]♦ I passed Mrs King-Brown in the street today but she cut me dead; I wonder what I've done to offend her.[/ex]
	
cut down
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 валить, рубить (деревья):[/trn]
	\[X9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ Half the forest was cut down to make room for the new road.[/ex] → get down (3)
	[m1][trn]2 ушивать, укорачивать (одежду); сокращать (рукопись и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ I could cut your father's trousers down for the boy. Your article will have to be cut down to fit into the book.[/ex] 
	—cut-down [p]adj[/p] → make down 
	[m1][trn]3 [p]not fml[/p] сокращать (что-л.), особ. в целях экономии:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The factory's production has been cut down.[/ex] → cut back (4), cut down on
	[m1][trn]4 убить (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. pass.)\] [ex]♦ The soldier was cut down in his youth.[/ex] → cut off (8)
	[m1][trn]5 [p]not fml[/p] разбить (аргумент):[/trn] 
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Your arguments are too easy to cut down.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 [p]not fml[/p] сразить (кого-л.); поставить (кого-л.) на место:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Jim was beginning to argue wildly again, getting his facts wrong, so his father cut him down.[/ex] → cut down to (2)
	[m1][trn]7 убедить (кого-л.) снизить цену:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (by, to) [/com]\] [ex]♦ He's asking too much for the chairs, can't you cut him down? In the end I cut the dealer down by another £3.00.[/ex]
	
cut down on
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	→ cut back (4), cut down (3)[p] 
	[m1][trn]not fml[/p] сокращать (что-л.), обыкн. по необходимости, напр., в целях экономии:[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass.)\] [ex]♦ The factory cannot afford to employ any more workers, so it will have to cut down on production.[/ex]
	\[T4\] [ex]♦ In these times of rising prices, we must all cut down on our spending. The doctor advised Father to cut down on smoking.[/ex]
	
cut down to
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m0][p]v prep[/p] 
	→ cut down (7)
	[m1][trn]1 заставлять (кого-л.) снизить цену:[/trn]
	\[T1 + (о\] [ex]♦ We were able to cut the dealer down to £3 25.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 cut someone down to size поставить (кого-л.) на место, сбить (с кого-л.) спесь:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The director is too proud, he needs to be cut down to size.[/ex]
	→ cut down (6)
	
cut fine
	[p]v adj[/p]
	cut it fine
	[m1][trn]1 едва успеть, чуть не опоздать:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ You've cut it fine, haven't you? The train's just leaving.[/ex]
	→ cut short (4)
	[m1][trn]2 [p]AmE[/p] очень точно рассчитать что-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ This answer is correct to the last cent; you've cut it (very) fine.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 улавливать почти невидимую разницу между похожими вещами:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Hut the two meanings are almost exactly the same; aren't you cutting it rather fine, saying they should be separated?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 оставлять себе денег в обрез:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ By the time we've paid the bill we have $42 left, which I call cutting it a bit fine.[/ex]
	
cut for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]выниманием карт определить (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + for[/com]\] [ex]♦ First, we cut for dealer, then begin the game. Aren't we going to cut for who has the first turn?[/ex]
	
cut free
	[p]v adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 освободить, высвободить (что-л., кого-л. или животное):[/trn]
	\[Х7 + free (/rent)\] [ex]♦ Cut the boat free, we're ready to sail. Firemen were called to the scene of the accident to cut the driver free from the wreck of his car. Cut the poor dog free quickly, his neck is caught in the rope![/ex] → cut loose (1)
	[m1][trn]2 освобождать(ся) (от чего-л. или кого-л.), вырваться:[/trn]
	\[Т1b (from)\] [ex]♦ The painter cut himself free from family responsibilities and went to live on a tropical island.[/ex] → cut loose (2).
	
cut from
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отрубать, обрубать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ If you cut a branch from this tree, it can grow into a new tree.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 сокращать, урезывать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ You will have to cut about twenty pages from your book, it's too long.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 cut the ground from under someone's feet [p]not fml[/p] выбить почву у кого-л. из-под ног:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The Opposition had been telling the voters about the government's inaction, but the government then cut the ground from under their feet by doing the right things just before the election.[/ex]
	
cut in
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 добавлять (что-л.), осторожно перемешивая ножом и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[Х9 + IN\] [ex]♦ Mix the sugar and butter, then cut the flour in with a knife or spoon.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 вклинивать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[X9 + IN\] [ex]♦ We'll cut in the piece of film that we have already made. Here is where you cut this new wire in.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [p]not fml[/p] вмешиваться (в чью-л. беседу и т. п), перебивать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (on) (usu. simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ "May I join you?" a loud voice cut in. I was enjoying the dance until that rude man cut in. Don't cut in on other people's conversations.[/ex]
	→ break in (3), burst in (3)
	[m1][trn]4 внезапно появляться перед кем-л. или перед автомобилем, вклиниваться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (on) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ We were driving peacefully along the road when this red car cut in (on us), forcing us to slow down. I had been waiting behind six other people for the bus, when this fat woman cut in (in front of me).[/ex]
	→ cut ahead of
	[m1][trn]5 [p]infml[/p] включать (кого-л. в карточную игру, в дело и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (on) (usu. simple tenses)[/ex][/com]\] [ex]♦ Would you like to join our card game? I can cut you in. The chief buyer says he can cut you in (on the deal).[/ex]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	→ cut into (1), divide in 
	[m1][trn]разрезать, делить (что-л. частями):[/trn]
	\[T1 + in\] [ex]♦ Cut the cake in four and share it equally. The car was cut in half in the crash.[/ex]
	
cut into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 разрезать, делить (что-л. на части):[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 + into[/com]\] [ex]♦ Cut the cake into quarters and share it equally. The ship was cut into several pieces in the accident.[/ex]
	→ cut in2, divide into, separate into
	[m1][trn]2 начать резать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[L9 + into\] Mother said we could cut into the new cake.[/ex] → slice into
	[m1][trn]3 перебивать (что-л.):[/trn]
