	[m1][trn]1 возвращаться тем же путём:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ If you get lost in a forest, it is best to double back the way you came.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 складывать (что-л.) вдвое, сгибать, загибать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Double the тар back so that we can read it more easily. We double the top of the sheet back over the covers, for comfortable sleep.[/ex]
	→ fold back, etc.
	
double for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	→ stand in for, etc.
	[m1][trn]замещать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Who will double for the secretary while he is on holiday? I'll double for you in the committee meeting.[/ex]
	
double in
double in brass
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p]AmE[/p] уметь играть на ещё одном духовом инструменте, кроме основного:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Can any of the players double in brass?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]AmE infml[/p] знать какую-л. работу так же хорошо, как и свою специальность:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I think we should appoint the younger man, because he can double in brass by writing as well as printing the magazine.[/ex]
	
double over
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 складывать (что-л.) вдвое, сгибать, загибать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Double the тар over so that we can read it more easily.[/ex]
	→ fold back, etc.
	[m1][trn]2 согнуть(ся) пополам от боли, хохота и т. п.:[/trn] 
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Mary doubled over when Jim walked in wearing his funny clothes. The fighter doubled over at the sudden heavy blow.
	\[[/ex]T1\] [ex]♦ We found grandfather in his chair, doubled over with pain. The blow doubled the fighter over.[/ex] → double up (2), etc.
	
double up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 складывать (что-л.) вдвое:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We shall have to double up the sheets to get them in the drawer.[/ex] 
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ This mat is too thick to double up.[/ex]
	→ fold back, etc.
	[m1][trn]2 согнуть(ся) пополам от боли, хохота и т. п.[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Mary doubled up when Jim walked in wearing his funny clothes. The fighter doubled up at the sudden heavy blow.[/ex]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We found grandfather in his chair, doubled up with pain. The blow doubled the fighter up. The joke doubled the crowd up.[/ex] → crack up (5), crease up (3), crumple up (5), curl up (4), double over (2), fold up (3)
	[m1][trn]3 [p]not fml[/p] увеличивать количество, особ. проживающих или спящих; делить (с кем-л.) комнату или постель:[/trn] 
	\[IØ (wM)\] [ex]♦ When all the family are here for Christmas, the children will have to double up in one room. Do you mind doubling up with Jane tonight?[/ex]
	
double with
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	→ double as
	[m1][trn]играть две роли в одном спектакле:[/trn]
	\[Х9 + м7А\] [ex]♦ In the play 'Hamlet,' it is usual for an actor to double the first gravedigger with the spirit of Hamlet's father.[/ex]
	
doubt of
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[p]fml[/p]
	[m1][trn]сомневаться (в чём-л.):[/trn]
