	\[L9 + at[/ex]\][ex]♦ It's so annoying, the way he keeps dragging at his pipe.[/ex]
	
drag away
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 оттягивать, оттаскивать (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn] 
	\[[com]Х9 + AWAY (from)[/com]\] [ex]♦ It will take two elephants to drag all this wood away. His mother dragged the child away from the fire just in time.[/ex]
	→ drag off, jerk away, pull away (1), take away (1), yank away
	[m1][trn]2 с трудом заставить (кого-л.) покинуть (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn] 
	\[[com]T1b (from)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Have you ever tried dragging a child away from a television set? How can I drag myself away from your arms?[/ex]
	→ pull away (4), tear away (3)
	
drag behind
	[p]v adv; prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отставать, тащиться позади:[/trn]
	\[L9 + BEHIND/Mwtd\] [ex]♦ Don't drag behind (the others), you'll make us all late.[/ex] → lag behind (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 не дотягивать (до уровня чего-л.), отставать (по качеству работы и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[L9 + BEHIND/fteAind\] [ex]♦ Your work has been dragging behind (the general standard) recently, you'll have to do better.[/ex]
	→ fall behind2 (3), etc.
	
drag down
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 тащить (что-л.) вниз:[/trn]
	\[T1 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ The box is too heavy to carry down the slope, we'll have to drag it down.[/ex] pull down (2) 
	[m1][trn]2 делать (кого-л.) слабым, как после болезни:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ It's the fever that's been dragging him down.[/ex] → pull down (4)
	[m1][trn]3 понижать социальный статус (кого-л.), разрушать (кого-л.) морально; губить (кого-л. ):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ If you marry that man, he'll drag you down.[/ex]
	→ pull down (5)
	
drag in
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 втаскивать (кого-л. или что-л.), затаскивать (кого-л. или что-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + IN\] [ex]♦ The children are so busy playing that they don't want their dinner, you'll have to drag them in. You look like something the cat dragged in.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]not fml[/p] приводить (замечание, аргумент и т. п.) без связи с темой разговора, притягивать за уши:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ There's по need to keep dragging in my father's opinion, it has nothing to do with your argument.[/ex]
	→ drag up (2)
	
drag into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 втаскивать, затаскивать (кого-л. или что-л. куда-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + into[/com]\] [ex]♦ You'll have to drag the children into the house, they're too busy playing to want their dinner. The farmer had to drag the unwilling cow into the field.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]not fml[/p] втягивать, вовлекать (кого-л. во что-л.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Don't try to drag me into your plans.[/ex]
	\[V4b\] [ex]♦ I was dragged into helping with the concert.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 притянуть (тему в разговор):[/trn]
