fall away
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 отрываться от чего-л.; отпадать:[/trn]
	\[L9 + AWAY\] [ex]♦ Be careful on this part of the slope, bits of rock have fallen away.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 понижаться; опускаться; обрываться вниз:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + AWAY (to) (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The cliff fell away at his feet.[/ex]
	→ drop away (1), drop off (2), fall off1 (2)
	[m1][trn]3 уменьшаться, ослабевать:[/trn]
	\[IØ (to)\] [ex]♦ Student numbers have been falling away recently. Interest in the game has fallen away (almost to nothing).[/ex] → drop away (2), drop off (4), fall off1 (3)
	[m1][trn]4 становиться хуже, ухудшаться:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ The standard of your work has been falling away recently.[/ex] → drop away (3), drop off (5), fall behind1 (3), fall off1 (4), go off1 (7)
	[m1][trn]5 спадать, ослабевать, уменьшаться; исчезать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The wind fell away and all was calm. His smile fell away when he saw who his visitor was. When the brother and sister met again at last, the years of absence fell away and soon they were talking as if they had never been apart. All doubt fell away and we knew we would be victorious.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 переставать оказывать поддержку, откалываться:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Some of our formerly loyal members have fallen away.[/ex] → fall off (5)
	[m1][trn]7 похудеть, осунуться:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Her face has fallen away since she lost weight.[/ex] → fall in1 (3)
	[m1][trn]8 [p]naut[/p] уваливаться; не слушаться руля:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The leading boat fell away when the wind grew too strong. "Fall away!" ordered the captain.[/ex]
	→ fall off1 (6), pay off (6), sag away
	[m1][trn]9 направлять самолет прочь из группы других, образующих фигуру, линию и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The planes rose into the sky in a V-shape; then the leaders fell away and the others followed.[/ex]
	
fall back
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 падать назад, на спину:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + BACK (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I fell back and hurt my head. The traveller fell back into the comfortable chair, tired out.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 падать, снижаться:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + BACK (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Beyond the mouth of the river, the shore line falls back.[/ex]
