	\[L4 (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ I never dreamed that I would fetch up owning such a lot of property! Be careful, you could fetch up by getting hurt.[/ex] → end up (2), finish up (3), land up (4), wind up (7)
	[m1][trn]6 esp. [p]BrE infml[/p] попадать (куда-л.); оказываться (где-л.):[/trn]
	\[L9 (at, in, on) (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ When Jim's driving, we never know where we'll fetch up. He'll fetch up in prison if he goes on taking risks like that. The boy's ball fetched up on the garage roof.[/ex] → end up (3), finish up (4), land up (5), wind up (8)
	[m1][trn]7 esp. [p]BrE infml[/p] попадать в (неприятное положение и т. п.); плохо кончить:[/trn]
