	[m1][trn]1 дышать с трудом, задыхаться от усталости, изумления и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + for (often continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ After running such a long way, the messenger was gasping for breath. Gasping for air, the firemen fought their way through clouds of smoke. Her unexpected rudeness made me gasp for breath. What a hot day! I'm gasping for a cold drink, aren't you? [/ex]
	→ pant for (1)
	[m1][trn]2 страстно желать (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Give me a cigarette, will you? I'm gasping for a smoke. For a long time, she's been gasping for a chance to show her acting ability, and now her chance has come![/ex]
	→ pant for (2).
	
gasp out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 задохнуться (от потрясения и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + OUT (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ He gasped out when he read the letter.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 произносить (что-л.) задыхаясь:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The messenger gasped out his story after running all the way from the battle.[/ex] pant out.
	
gather from
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 собирать (напр., зерно, орехи где-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ These little animals gather nuts from the ground in the autumn, and store them for the winter.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 появляться (откуда-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ Every time there is an accident, a crowd seems to gather from nowhere.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 понять (по чему-л.), извлечь (из чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ What did you gather from his letter?[/ex]
	\[[com]T5 + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ Do I gather from the look on your face that you're not pleased with the result? He did not make his intentions clear, but I gathered from what little he did say that he did not want to employ me.[/ex] understand by.
	
gather in
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 собирать и убирать (в хранилище) созревший урожай:[/trn]
	\[T1 + IN\] [ex]♦ When all the crops are safely gathered in, the farmers can rest.[/ex]
	→ garner in
	[m1][trn]2 собирать (материал) в сборки, складки при шитье:[/trn]
	\[T1 + IN\] [ex]♦ Gather the waist in a little more, with fine stitches.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 собирать, получать; скапливать (что-л., напр., деньги):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Some of the workers think that big business directors don't do any work, but just sit in their offices gathering in the profits.[/ex]
	
gather round
	[p]v adv; prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 собирать(ся) (вокруг кого-л. или чего-л.), подходить ближе (к кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[IØ + ROUND\] [ex]♦ Gather round, ladies and gentlemen, and see this wonderful new invention.[/ex]
	\[[com]IØ + round[/com]\] [ex]♦ A small crowd gathered round the speaker to hear what he had to say.[/ex]
	\[[com]T1 + round[/com]\] [ex]♦ The speaker gathered a small crowd round him, eager to listen to what he had to say. The boy gathered his toys round him selfishly.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 приходить на помощь (кому-л.):[/trn] 
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ The party members gathered round when their leader was attacked.[/ex]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The whole class gathered round the student who had been unfairly failed, and demanded a reexamination.[/ex]
	
gather to
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 привлекать (кого-л. куда-л.), собирать (что-л. где-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + to[/com]\] [ex]♦ We must gather the people to our side. The dressmaker gathered the cloth to the narrowest part of the waist.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 be gathered to one's fathers [p] fml euph[/p] умереть; отправиться к праотцам:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. perfect tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ We must not be too sad that our muchloved king has been gathered to his fathers.[/ex]
	
gather together
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 собирать(ся); образовывать толпу, группу и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[IØ + TOGETHER\] [ex]♦ Cows tend to gather together at one end of a field when it is going to rain.[/ex]
	\[T1 + TOGETHER\] [ex]♦ Gather the ends of the wool together and tie them in a knot. Give me a few minutes to gather my thoughts together. We must gather the people together to demand our rights.[/ex] → get together (1)
	[m1][trn][b]2 gather oneself together[/b]взять себя в руки, держать себя под контролем:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I shall have to gather myself together to face the whole board of directors.[/ex]
	→ get together (8), pull together [b](4)[/b].
	
gather up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 собирать; поднимать, подбирать; убирать в одно место (обыкн. вещи):[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP) [ex]♦ Gathering up his scattered papers, he pushed them into his case.[/ex]
	→ pick up (1)
	[m1][trn]2 собраться; напрягать (мышцы):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Gather up your muscles and jump.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 подтянуться, собраться с силами:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Gathering up all his courage, he turned to face the enemy.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [b]gather up the threads[/b][p]not fml[/p] возобновлять, восстанавливать (работу и т. п.), вернуться к жизни:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Several books that were very important for my work were lost in the fire, and it's going to be hard to gather up the threads.[/ex] → pick up (26)
	
