get along
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 продвигать(ся):[/trn]
	\[L9 + ALONG\] [ex]♦ The car could hardly get along on the icy surface.[/ex]
	\[X9 + ALONG\] [ex]♦ A hot drink will help to get you along on this cold night.[/ex] → get along with (1), get on with (1), go along with (1)
	[m1][trn]2 посылать или брать (что-л. или кого-л.); доставлять:[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + ALONG (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I'll get your clothes along to you as soon as you have a fixed address. You'd better get the boy along to a hospital, that wound looks bad.[/ex]
	→ come along (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 [p]not fml[/p] уходить; уезжать; убираться:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ I think I'll be getting along now, I want to be home quite early. Get along, you boys! I don't want you here![/ex]
	→ get along with (5), go along with (5)
