	→ come at (4)
	[m1][trn]3 работать над (чем-л.), напр., после перерыва, отсрочки и т. п.; приниматься за (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I'll go into the office early tomorrow so as to have time to get at that pile of work that's been waiting for me.[/ex]
	\[T4\] [ex]♦ I'd like to get at repainting the house as soon as the weather is suitable.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [p]not fml[/p] иметь в виду:[/trn]
	\[What + T1 (no pass., continuous tenses)\] [ex]♦ What are you getting at?[/ex] → be at (1), drive at (3)
	[m1][trn]5 [p]not fml[/p] подкупать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[ V3\] [ex]♦ The prisoners escaped after getting at the guards to leave the gate open.[/ex]
	\[T1 (often pass.)\] [ex]♦ Policemen in this country cannot be got at.[/ex] → get to (8)
	[m1][trn]6 [p]not fml[/p] ругать; раздражать (кого-л.); придираться (к кому-л.), приставать (к кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ She's always getting at the children for one thing or another. I feel I'm being got at.[/ex]
	\[V3 (usu. continuous tenses)\] [ex]♦ Stop getting at me to clean my shoes, I'll do them tonight.[/ex] → go on at (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]7 портить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Someone's been getting at my drink, it tastes strange. The thieves tried to get at the lock, but it was too strongly made.[/ex] → meddle with (1), etc.
	
get away
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 уезжать, уходить, выбираться:[/trn]
