	\[L9 + AWAY (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ This new car gets away faster than any of our former models. The runners have got away and the long race has begun.[/ex] → be off (4), get off1 (6)
	[m1][trn]4 забирать (что-л. или кого-л.); вынимать, вытаскивать (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + AWAY\] (from) (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I couldn't get the children away fast enough; that school was a terrible place. The axe was stuck in the tree, but I pulled hard and got it away.[/ex]
	→ send away (1), take away (2)
	[m1][trn]5 удрать, ускользнуть, улизнуть, напр., с места преступления; сбежать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ You should have seen the size of the fish that got away! Two thieves got away.[/ex] 
	—getaway [p] n, adj.[/p]
	[m1][trn]6 get away (with you) [p]infml[/p] я тебе не верю!, ну да!, брось свои шуточки!:[/trn]
	\[[com] imper[/com]\] [ex]♦ Oh, get away (with you)! I know better than that! Get away! I would never have thought it! [/ex]→ come on (10), etc.
	
get away from
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 убежать, удрать от (чего-л. или кого-л.); забрать (что-л., кого-л. откуда-л.), убрать (что-л. от кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + AWAY + from (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The prisoners got away from their guards after a struggle. I couldn't get away from her at the party; she just kept talking![/ex] \[X9 + AWAY +from (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Can't you get your child away from that terrible school? Get those matches away from the baby![/ex] → take away from (1, 2), take from (1)
	[m1][trn]2 избегать; не обращать внимания на (что-л. неприятное):[/trn]
