	\[T4 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ You can't get away with being late every morning.[/ex]
	→ get by with (3)
	[m1][trn]6 отделаться менее строгим наказанием:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The men went to prison but the two boys got away with a warning.[/ex]
	→ get off with (2), let off1 (3)
	[m1][trn]7 get away with murder остаться безнаказанным за серьёзный проступок, правонарушение; выйти сухим из воды:[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ That teacher is most unfair; some students are punished for the least little thing, while others who are her favourites can get away with murder.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 get away with you [p]infml[/p] я тебе не верю!, да ну тебя!, иди ты!:[/trn]
