get to
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 приходить, приезжать, добираться (куда-л.); доставлять:[/trn]
	\[L9 + to (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ What time does this train get to l-ondon? What time do you usually get to bed?[/ex]
	\[[com]X9 + to (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The boat will only get you to the nearest island, you have to make your own way from there. This old car may not run very well, but it gets me to work.[/ex]
	→ go to (1), send to (1), take to (1)
	[m1][trn]2 исчезать, пропадать (где-л.):[/trn] 
	\[L9 + to (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦Where did you get to? I've been looking for you everywhere. I don't know where my ring has got to, and I think it must have been stolen.[/ex] → become of, come of (1), disappear to, go to (5)
	[m1][trn]3 доходить, добираться (до какого-л. места в книге и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[L9 + to (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦Where have you got to in the book? I've got to the middle bit where the murderer is threatening the husband. The talks had to stop when they got to the point where we were all wasting our time and effort. Their argument got to the stage of pointless bad temper.[/ex] → get up to (2), go up to (7), take up to
	[m1][trn]4 доставлять, приводить, приносить (что-л. или кого-л. к кому-л. или куда-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + to (usu. simple tenses)) We have to get the book to the printer's this week. Getting the children to school in winter is much more worrying. I must rush and get this letter to the post before it's collected.[/ex] → send to (2), take to (1) 
	[m1][trn]5 начинать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ We must get to work at once (on the new building plans).[/ex]
	\[[com]T4 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Recently I've got to wondering why I am in this job.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 [p]not fml[/p] быть понятым (кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I've tried to help the troublesome boy but I can't seem to get to him.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 [p]not fml[/p] растрогать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ His sad story really got to me, and I was moved to help him.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 [p]AmE not fml[/p] подкупать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Somebody must have been getting to the guards; the doors were all unlocked.[/ex] 
	\[V3\] [ex]♦ The prisoners escaped after getting to the guards to leave the gate open.[/ex] → get at (5)
	[m1][trn]9 get access to получить доступ к (чему-л. или кому-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Two newspapermen got access to the politician's private papers and showed the public that he had acted criminally. The directors of the television stations decided that the public must be allowed to get access to television time and produce their own broadcasts.[/ex] → have to (1)
	[m1][trn]10 get to the bottom of добраться до сути (чего-л.); раскрыть (что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The owner of the jewels called in the police to get to the bottom of the mystery of the robbery.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]11 get to one's feet вставать, подниматься:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ At the end of the game, the whole crowd got to their feet and cheered wildly.[/ex]
	→ be on (Ila), bring to (9), come to (21), get on2 (4), keep on (8), remain on2 (3), rise to (5), stay on (4)
	[m1][trn]12 get to first base (with) esp. [p] AmE not fml[/p] начать (с чего-л.); преодолеть первую ступень (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. neg.[/com]\] [ex]♦ Anybody trying to start a new business in these hard times probably won't even get to first base. We never even got to first base with our plans for improving the conditions in the factory.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]13 get to grips with вступить в борьбу (с кем-л.), расправиться с чем-л.; подойти к разрешению (проблемы и т. п.): 
	[ex]♦ Our soldiers are anxious to get to grips with the enemy. The government has promised to get to grips with the question of rising prices.[/ex]
	→ bring to2 (11), come to2 (24)
	[m1][trn]14 get to the point дойти до сути дела в речи, письме:[/trn] 
