	\[[com]T1b (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The United Nations should get Foreign Ministers together more often, to settle international disagreements by peaceful talks.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 объединяться, особ. для оплаты чего-л.:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ All the villagers got together and soon raised enough money for a swimming pool.
	\[[/ex]V3\] [ex]♦ The shopkeepers got together to put up Christmas lights so as to attract trade.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [p]infml[/p] достигать согласия; прийти к соглашению:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ I'm glad to see that the two firms have got together at last. Whether the two great powers will ever get together, is impossible to say.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 [p]not fml[/p] встречаться, собираться вместе:[/trn]
