get up to
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 добираться (куда-л.), достигать (чего-л.), поравняться с кем-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + UP + to (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The boy was too small to get up to the top branches. When I got up to her, I could see that she was a stranger after all.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 доходить, добираться до (какого-л. места в книге и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ What page have you got up to? I've got up to Part Three. The history lessons get up to the year 1642 and then stop. The temperature got up to 32' by 9 o'clock.[/ex]
	→ get to (3), go up to (7), take up to
	[m1][trn]3 вставать, подниматься утром с постели под звуки (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I like to get up to soft music, not shouting voices.[/ex]
	→ get up (5), get up with (1)
	[m1][trn]4 достигать определённого уровня; доводить до стандарта:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You need more practice to get up to performance.[/ex]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Some additional lessons might get you up to the standard demanded by the examiners.[/ex]
	→ be up to (4), bring up to (4), come up to (4, 5) 
	[m1][trn]5 затевать, замышлять (что-л. дурное или смешное):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Whatever will the students get up to next? Has that cat been getting up to its silly tricks again?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 get up to date (with) совершенетвовать свои знания, идти в ногу со временем:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Mother, you must get more up to date with modern styles! You can't wear that thing! I want to spend this weekend getting my letter writing up to date.[/ex]
	→ be out of (7), etc.
	[m1][trn]7 get up to mischief [p]not fml[/p] проказничать, шалить; откалывать номера:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Children get up to mischief if left alone for very long. That dog has been up to mischief again, jumping the fence and chasing the sheep.[/ex] → be up to (9).
	
