give up to
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 сдать, выдать (кого-л. кому-л.); уступать (что-л. кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + to (often simple tenses) [ex]♦ The gunman gave himself up to the police. The councillors refused to give up the town records to the enemy. When will the desert give up its secrets to mankind? It's still polite to give up your seat to an old lady.[/ex]
	→ give over to (1), yield to (1)
	[m1][trn]2 отдать (помещение кому-л. для чего-л.); посвятить (время кому-л. или чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The house was given up to the children for their parties during the season. The building was given up to the youth club by the church.[/ex]
	\[V4b\] [ex]♦ The rest of the evening will be given up to singing and dancing.[/ex]
	→ give over to (2)
	[m1][trn]3 посвятить (себя, своё время, жизнь и т. п.) полностью (чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (often simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Не has given himself up to a life of crime. The scientist gave himself up to a study of the life history of flies.[/ex]
	\[V4b (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ The doctor gave his life up to helping the poor natives.[/ex] → give over to (3)
	[m1][trn]4 предаваться (отчаянию и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Don't give yourself up to sadness, there's still hope![/ex] → give in to (3), give over to (4), give to (23), surrender to (2), yield to (3).
	
