	\[L9 + through (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ The piano won't go through this narrow entrance, it will have to come in through the window. We've been through banks of snow three metres high![/ex] → get through2 (1), take through (1)
	[m1][trn]2 [i] (о законе и т. п.)[/i] проходить (через парламент и т. п ):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass.)\] [ex]♦ The new law should go through Parliament quite easily, as it has been demanded by the public for some time.[/ex] → get through2 (3), put through2 (3), take through (3)
	[m1][trn]3 проходить (какие-л. ступени, этапы и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Your suggestion has to go through several stages. Tom's book has gone through three printings. Has the new law gone through all its stages yet?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 распространяться (где-л. или среди группы людей):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ A wild story has been going through the office, that the director's wife has left him. The disease went through the school like a wind.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 просить одобрения, санкции (кого-л.); иметь дело (с кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ If you want а special favour, you have to go through the director. All complaints have to go through Head Office.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 пережить (что-л.), перенести (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Не has gone through such a lot since his wife died. After all he's been through, he still keeps so cheerful![/ex]
	→ pass through2 (4)
	[m1][trn]7 повторять; заучивать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Go through your story again from the beginning, let's go through that scene again until you're sure you know it. I want to go through the wedding arrangements to make sure that nothing's been missed.[/ex] → go over2 (2), look over2 (5), run over2 (5), run through2 (7), take over2 (3), take through2 (2)
	[m1][trn]8 просматривать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We must go through the account books together; there's still some money missing. I've been through your report, and it looks quite satisfactory.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 осматривать (что-л.), обыскивать (что-л.):[/trn]
