	→ get off1 (14), take off1 (14)
	[m1][trn]5 имитировать, подражать, воспроизводить:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1b (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The boy had the teacher off to perfection.[/ex]
	→ hit off (1), take off1 (15) 
	[m1][trn]6 have it off [p] sl[/p] иметь тайные или незаконные интимные отношения (с кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[(usu. continuous tenses) \] [ex]♦ Jim and Mary were having it off long before they were married, I'm sure! I suppose you've been having it off with your friend' while I've been out of town! People are whispering that the director has been having it off with his secretary.[/ex] → have away
	
have on
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 быть одетым (во что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + ON (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Mary had on her best blue dress. Can you tell us what the missing woman had on? Don't come in! I've nothing on![/ex]
