	\[simple tenses\] [ex]♦ What bearing does your story have on this case? The examination results have no bearing on your ability.[/ex] bear on (1), touch on (3) 
	[m1][trn]5 have something/someone on the brain [p]not fml[/p] постоянно думать о чём-л. или ком-л.; не мочь забыть что-л. или кого-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Have you ever had a tune on your brain, going round and round and you couldnt stop it? Peter has cars on the brain, he never talks about anything else. Grace says that she can't forget her red-haired boy and will probably have him on the brain for the rest of her life.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 have a crush/pash on [p]infml[/p] сильно увлечься (кем-л.), обыкн. в юности, глупо влюбиться (в кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Some of the girls have a crush on one of the teachers.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 have designs on/against/upon [p]infml[/p] вынашивать планы добиться (чего-л. или кого-л.), часто нечестным путём; нацелиться (на что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I think that man has designs on my daughter. One of the committee members has designs on the chairmanship.[/ex]
