	\[T1\] [ex]♦ It's time we were able to lay off these heavy winter clothes.[/ex] → cast aside (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]9 [p]AmE not fml[/p] размечать, отмерять:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ First, lay off the size of the picture. Care must be taken to lay off the land in broad divisions.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 засевать (поле другой культурой):[/trn]
	\[T1 (into)\] [ex]♦ Some of the farmers are laying off their fields, after a very few crops of corn, into grass.[/ex] → lay down (6), put down (15)
	[m1][trn]11 [i] (в футболе)[/i] перепасовывать (мяч) на короткое расстояние:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Keegan laid the ball off for Channon to shoot.[/ex]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p]not fml[/p] прекратить, перестать (делать что-л.); бросить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The doctor advised Jim to lay off alcohol.[/ex]
	\[[com]T4 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ He also said that he should lay off smoking.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 уволить (кого-л.), обыкн. временно:[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ 500 men were laid off work when the factory closed after the fire.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [p]infml[/p] перестать надоедать (кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., simple tenses, often imper.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I jay off me, can't you? I've had enough of your unkind jokes![/ex]
	[m1][trn][b]4 lay one's fingers/hands off[/b][p]not fml[/p] не дотрагиваться до (чего-л. или кого-л.), держаться подальше от (чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn] 
	\[(usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Lay your fingers off that cake, I'm saving it for Jane's birthday. He'll learn the hard way to lay his hands off other men's wives.[/ex] → keep off (6).
	
lay on
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 проводить (воду, газ, электричество):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The house has water and electricity laid on.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [p]not fml[/p] снабжать (чем-л.), предоставлять (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The club laid on a special meal for the visitors. The government laid on a plane for the important visitor.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 налагать, вводить (налог, пошлину т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Further taxes may be laid on this spring.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 сыпать ударами; пускать в ход (кулаки):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (to)[/ex] [/com]\] [ex]♦ As he laid on blows to the boy's back, a man came up and took the whip out of his hand.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 [p] old use[/p] начинать бой:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ "lay on, Macduff."[/ex] (Shakespeare, [ex]♦ Macbeth) [/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 накладывать, наносить краску (особ. горизонтальными мазками):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Don! lay the colour on too thickly or the surface will not be smooth.[/ex]
	→ lay off1 (6)
	[m1][trn]7 lay it on (thick/with a trowel) [p]infml[/p] преувеличивать, перебарщивать; перехваливать:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Aren't you laying it on a bit thick? I'm sure the figures weren't quite as high as you say! "Well said: that was laid on with a trowel."[/ex] (Shakespeare. [ex]♦ As You Like It) [/ex]→ spread on1 (2)
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 положить, поместить на (что-л.); накладывать (краску и т. п.) на (что-л.):[/trn] 
	\[Х9 + on) [ex]♦ She laid her heavy case on the ground and took a rest. Three nurses helped to lay the unconscious boy on the operating table. She laid her hand comfortingly on mine. She laid a finger on her lips to signal silence. Help me to lay the new mat on the floor. The painter used a wide brush to lay his colours on the surface that he had prepared.[/ex] → lay with (1), place on (1), put on2 (1), set on2 (1)
	[m1][trn]2 налагать, навязывать:[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ The government has to lay heavy taxes on the people. When parents grow older, they lay a special duty on their children. Why are you trying to lay the blame on me?[/ex]
	→ fasten on2 (2), pin on2 (2), place on (2), put on2 (2), throw on2 (4)
	[m1][trn]3 ставить (деньги) на (что-л.), рисковать деньгами:[/trn]
	\[D1 (often simple tenses)) [ex]♦ I'm willing to lay good money on our team's victory.[/ex]
	→ place on (3), put on2 (7), set on2 (6)
	[m1][trn]4 lay a burden on взвалить на (кого-л.) бремя ответственности и т. п.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The President has expressed his willingness to accept the solemn burden of office that the voters have laid on him.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 lay one's cards on the table [p]not fml[/p] выложить свои карты на стол; раскрыть свои планы, намерения и т. п.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I see that it's time to lay my cards on the table: I am interested in this affair because the woman in the case is my sister.[/ex]
	→ place on (3), put on2 (II), set on2 (6)
	[m1][trn]6 lay emphasis/stress/weight on сделать акцент на (чём-л.), подчёркивать важность (чего-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ When giving the orders, the captain laid stress on the urgency of the work. The examination instructions lay emphasis on completing the correct number of questions in the limited time.[/ex]
	→ put on2 (13)
	[m1][trn]7 lay eyes on [p]not fml[/p] видеть (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Don't ask me where Jim is, I haven't laid eyes on him for weeks.[/ex]
	→ clap on2 (4), set on2 (7)
	[m1][trn]8 lay a finger/hand on [p]not fml[/p] дотронуться до (кого-л.), причинить вред (кому-л):[/trn] 
	(usu. simple tenses, neg. or in questions or conditional statements)\] [ex]♦ Don't you dare lay a finger on my son! If you lay a hand on me I shall send for the police![/ex]
	→ set on2 (9)
	[m1][trn]9 lay one's finger on [p]not fml[/p] определить причину (чего-л.), найти объяснение (чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[simple tenses, usu. neg.\] [ex]♦ I can't lay my finger on the reason for the student's sudden lack of interest.[/ex] → put on2 (16)
	[m1][trn]10 lay great/little store on высоко/низко оценивать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ My grandfather laid great store on his moral principles.[/ex]
	→ lay by2 (2), set by2 (2), set on2 (23)
	[m1][trn]11 lay one's hands on:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]a [p]not fml[/p] найти (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[simple tenses\] [ex]♦ I can't lay my hands on the account book — have you seen it?[/ex] → put on2 (19a) 
	[m1][trn]b [p]not fml[/p] достать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ I'd like to know where I can lay my hands on that special tobacco.[/ex]
	→ get on2 (8), put on2 (19b), set on2 (13) 
	[m1][trn]c [p]not fml[/p] схватить (что-л. или кого-л.); расправиться с (кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The police will soon lay their hands on the jewel thieves. I'd like to lay my hands on the man who attacked my daughter.[/ex]
	→ get on2 (9), put on2 (19c), set on2 (13) 
	[m1][trn]d [p]fml[/p] благословить (кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The bishop made a special visit to lay hands on a group of young people, so admitting them to membership of the Church,[/ex] 
	-laying-on of hands [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]12 lay hold on: 
	[m1][trn]a [p]not fml[/p] ухватиться за (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Lay hold on this rope and we'll pull you up.[/ex] → get of (5), lay of (1), take of (10) 
	[m1][trn]b достать (что-л.); найти (кого-л):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Where can I lay hold on this special tobacco?[/ex]
	→ get of (6), lay of (2)
	[m1][trn]13 lay one's hopes on возлагать надежды на (что-л.), надеяться на (что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Jim has laid all his hopes on winning this race. Don't lay your hopes on this job, you may not get it. [/ex]→ pin on2 (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]14 lay violent hands on oneself [p] old use[/p] наложить на себя руки, покончить с собой:[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ “Or have laid violent hands upon themselves.[/ex] ” (Book of Common Prayer)
	
lay open
	[p]v adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 поранить, порезать, повредить (часть тела):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + open (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The child fell off his bicycle and laid his face open.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 раскрыть, обнаружить; разгласить:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1a (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The firm's intentions were laid open by the director's accidental remark.[/ex]
	→ lay bare (2)
	[m1][trn]3 lay oneself open to открыться (для удара и т. п.), навлекать на себя (беду и т. п.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ By admitting that he had copied part of his article, the student laid himself open to a charge of cheating.[/ex]
	
lay out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [i](о виде)[/i] открываться взору; располагаться:[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. pass.)\] [ex]♦ The scenery was laid out before the travellers when they reached the top of the hill. All the family's pitiful possessions were laid out in the yard. The goods for sale were laid out attractively,[/ex] 
	—layout [p]n[/p] → set out (4)
	[m1][trn]2 выкладывать, вынимать (одежду, еду и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Please lay out my best suit for the governors' meeting. I'll leave a meal laid out in the kitchen.[/ex]
	→ drag out (1), get out (5), put out (3), set forth (3), set out (5)
	[m1][trn]3 (рас)планировать, располагать; разбивать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Laying out the page well makes all the difference to the ease of reading the book. 'The garden... was well laid out."[/ex] (Jane Austen. [i] Pride and Prejudice)[/i] 
	—layout [p]n[/p]
	→ set out (6)
	[m1][trn]4 [p]not fml[/p] тратить (деньги, силы и т. п.); рисковать (в денежных и т. п. операциях):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Having laid out his father's fortune into shares, he was able to live on the interest. I had to lay out all my strength to move the rock.[/ex] 
	—outlay [p]n[/p] → put out (19)
	[m1][trn]5 сбить с ног, вывести из строя; убить:[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ With one blow he laid his attacker out. Three of the enemy were laid out at once. I shall be laid out dead long before that happens![/ex] → knock out (3), etc.
	[m1][trn]6 сильно утомлять:[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ This heat has quite laid me out.[/ex] → tire out, etc.
	[m1][trn]7 приготовить к погребению:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Two of the women came to lay out the body.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 напрягаться, стараться изо всех сил:[/trn]
	\[V3\] [ex]♦ Mother was always willing to lay herself out to help people.[/ex]
	→ put out (15), etc.
	[m1][trn]9 [p]AmE infml[/p] ругать, бранить; придираться:[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ The director laid Jim out for being late again.[/ex] → tell off (1), etc.
	
