	\[[com]T1b (usu. simple tenses)[/ex][/com]\] [ex]♦ Lay the ship to outside the harbour.[/ex]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 lay something to someone's charge возлагать вину на кого-л.; считать кого-л. ответственным за что-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com] (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You don't want a terrible crime like that laid to your charge; tell the police that your companion did it![/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 lay claim to требовать, претендовать; предъявлять требование, претензию:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Both parents are trying to lay claim to the child. Several people have laid claim to the money that was found. The girl is laying claim to having swum across the lake.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 lay someone to rest/sleep [p] euph[/p] похоронить кого-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ She was laid to rest in the family grave.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 lay something to rest положить конец чс- му-л.; закончить что-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com] (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Her doubts were quickly laid to rest when he arrived as he had promised.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 lay siege to:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а осадить, взять в осаду (город):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The army laid siege to the town until the hungry citizens were forced to yield,[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b уломать, уговорить (кого-л.); заставить (сделать что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The only way to have the new law stopped is to lay siege to all the members of Parliament and persuade them to vote against it.[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]с настойчиво ухаживать, стараться добиться взаимности в любви:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Jim laid siege to Mary for a year before she agreed to marry him.[/ex]
	
lay together
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 складывать, помешать вместе:[/trn]
	\[X9 + TOGETHER\] [ex]♦ Don't lay the sticks too close together, or the fire will not burn well.[/ex] → put together (1)
	[m1][trn]2 lay our/your/their heads together [p]not fml[/p] думать вместе над (планом действий и т. п.), вместе обсуждать что-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Let's lay our heads together and see if we can invent a cheaper and better system.[/ex]
