	\[V4b\] [ex]♦ I'll let you off doing the dishes, as you helped with the shopping.[/ex]
	→ get out of (13), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 let someone off the hook [p]infml[/p] снять вину, тяжёлую обязанность и т. п. с кого-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The director accepted my explanation that the accident was not my fault, so I got let off the hook. When the judge let the boys off the hook, they were suitably grateful. Those three children were driving me mad until their mother came home and let me off the hook.[/ex]
	→ be off2 (8), be on2 (17), get off2 (12).
	
let on
	[p]v adv[/p]
