	[m1][trn]3 пропускать (воду), выпускать (воздух, газ):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + OUT (of)[/com]\] [ex]♦ It's a cruel joke to let the air out of somebody's car tyres. She let her breath out with a loud noise. There's a hole in the bottom of the bucket that lets the water out. It's good to let out your feelings in a shout,[/ex] 
	—outlet [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]4 издавать (звук, крик):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1a (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ He let out a cry of pain as the nail went into his foot.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 проговориться, проболтаться:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses') [/com]\] [ex]♦ The foolish young politician let out the date of the election in an unguarded moment.[/ex]
	\[[com]T5 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Mary accidentally let out that her mother had telephoned.[/ex]
	\[[com]T6 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Jane let out where she had hidden her father's birthday present.[/ex]
	→ be out (10), bring out (11), come out (12), filter out (4), get out (9), leak out (2)
	[m1][trn]6 [i](об огне)[/i] потухать:[/trn]
