	[m1][trn]3 look someone in the eye(s)/face [p]not fml[/p] смотреть прямо в глаза кому-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. neg., simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ I wonder you can look me in the face after the way you've behaved! She knew he was lying when he couldnt look her in the eyes.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 look a gift horse in the mouth [p]not fml[/p] смотреть в зубы дарёному коню:[/trn] 
	(usu. neg\] [ex]♦ I shan't complain about the poor view since the ticket was free; after all, you don't look a gift horse in the mouth.[/ex]
	
look into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 смотреть внутрь (чего-л.); вглядываться во (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + into[/com]\] [ex]♦ I looked into the room but no one was there. She looked into my eyes for a long time without speaking. I got such a shock when I looked into the mirror and saw the colour of my hair.[/ex]
	→ look in2 (1)
	[m1][trn]2 обращаться за информацией, справляться:[/trn]
