make for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 изготавливать; делать(ся) специально для (кого-л.), по специальному заказу:[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 + for[/com]\] [ex]♦ Не used to be so fat that he couldn't fit into any ready-made clothes, and had to have his suits made for him. It's time I made some new curtains for the living room.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 быстро продвигаться в направлении (чего-л.); спешно направляться (куда-л.):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Though badly damaged by fire, the ship tried to make for her home port. After the concert, the crowd made for the nearest door.[/ex]
	→ make towards
	[m1][trn]3 надвигаться, приближаться с угрожающим видом:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ When the thieves saw the big dog making for them, they ran away.[/ex]
	→ come after (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 способствовать, благоприятствовать (чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The large print makes for easier reading. Having different religions does not make for easy friendship. The plan might make for a good House of Lords.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 be made for быть предназначенным, созданным для (чего-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ These hills are made for winter sports. He seems made for politics. Jim and Mary seem to be made for one another.[/ex]
	→ mean for (2)
	[m1][trn]6 make allowance(s) for принимать во внимание, делать скидку на (что-л.); снисходительно отнестись к (кому-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The music judges were instructed to make allowance for the singer's inexperience. We'd better make allowance for some delay. I shall make allowances for you and not punish you this time.[/ex]
	→ allow for (2)
	[m1][trn]7 make amends for возмещать (ущерб и т. п.); компенеировать (что-л.):[/trn] 
