	[m1][trn]8 make arrangements for готовить, организовывать (что-л.); делать приготовления к (чему-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Have you made arrangements for a photographer to attend the wedding? Who is making arrangements for the next meeting?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 make a beeline for [p]not fml[/p] направляться прямиком (куда-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ soon as they reached the park, the young people made a beeline for the swimming pool.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 make a bid for: 
	[m1][trn]а предлагать цену на аукционе и т. п.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Did you make a bid for the painting? Yes, but somebody else offered more. [/ex]
	[m1][trn]b претендовать на (что-л.), стремиться к достижению (чего-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Will Jim make a bid for the big prize this year? The politician is making a bid for the women's vote. The prisoner made a bid for freedom, but was caught.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]11 make a bolt/break for it [p]not fml[/p] пытаться бежать; совершать побег:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Two prisoners have made a bolt for it, and the guards are searching for them in the hills.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 make a bolt/dash for [p]not fml[/p] помчаться к (чему-л.), пытаясь убежать; пытаться бежать:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ While the guard's back was turned, the prisoner made a bolt for the open door.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]13 make a long arm for [p]not fml[/p] тянуться за (чем-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Why make a long arm for the salt? I would have passed it to you.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]14 make a name for oneself [p]not fml[/p] стать известным, популярным:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ It's difficult to make a name for yourself on the concert stage, where the competition is so strong.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]15 make a play for esp. [p]AmE infml[/p] пытаться добиться (чего-л. или чьего-л. расположения); ухаживать за (кем-л.):[/trn] 
