	[m1][trn]26 make head (n)or tail of [p]not fml[/p] понять (кого-л. или что-л.), разобраться в (чём-л. или ком-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] simple tenses, with can, neg.[/com]\] [ex]♦ I can't make head or tail of this map; how can we be expected to find our way? He's a strange character; I can't make head nor tail of him.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]27 make heavy weather of [p]not fml[/p] преувеличивать трудность (работы, выполнения чего-л.); с большим трудом, напряжением исполнять (что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ You seem to be making heavy weather of this piece of music; it's actually quite easy. Why is she making such heavy weather of telephoning her mother?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]28 make an honest woman of [p]not fml[/p] узаконить свои отношения с женщиной; жениться на своей любовнице:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ We've been living together for six months; when are you going to make an honest woman of me?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]29 make light of[/trn]
	→ MAKE LIGHT OF
	[m1][trn]30 make light work of делать (что-л.) с лёгкостью; пара пустяков:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ With their experience, the men made light work of moving the heavy furniture. It was a difficult job, but he made light work of it.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]31 make a man of сделать настоящим мужчиной:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ ‘The regular army will make a man of you!'[/ex] (advertisement)
	[m1][trn]32 make a match of it быть хорошей супружеской парой, подходить друг другу в семейной жизни:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ "I had always supposed that you and Mrs Lupin would make a match of it." [/ex](Charles Dickens, [i] Martin Chuzzlewit[/i])
	[m1][trn]33 make a meal of: 
	[m1][trn]а считать (что-л.) достаточной, настоящей едой:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I can make a meal [/ex]of [ex]♦ a banana,[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b [p]infml[/p] перестараться:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The chairman is certainly making a meal of his goodbye speech! Going to a different play every night is, I consider, making a meal of it.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]34 make a mental note of взять на заметку; запомнить:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I made a mental note of his name, so as to avoid him in future. Make a mental note of the position of the tree, so that we can find our way back.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]35 make mention of [p]fml[/p] упомянуть (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ I must already have made mention of the people who were so kind to me on my travels. Mention has been made of the importance of considering the cost.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]36 make mincemeat of [p]not fml[/p] разбить в пух и прах; нанести сокрушительное поражение:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I'm afraid the other team made mincemeat of us; it was a terrible defeat. Our army made mincemeat of the enemy, and we won an important victory.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]37 make a mockery/travesty of превращать (что-л.) в фарс; опошлить (хорошее начинание и т. п.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Buying votes makes a mockery of free elections. The judge's treatment of the prisoner made a mockery of justice.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]38 make the most of использовать (что-л.) в полной мере; выжать всё из (чего-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Маке the most of the sunshine, we don't get much in the winter. Let's make the most of having the car for the day, and go for a long drive.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]39 make much of:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а понять (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. neg., usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ I didn't make much of his speech, did you?[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b придавать (чему-л.) слишком большое значение; гордиться (чем-л. или кем-л.); относиться к (кому-л.) с повышенным вниманием:[/trn]
	\[[com] usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Don't make too much of her rudeness, she's just a silly old woman. He likes to make much of the property he owns in different countries. Music has always been made much of in this school. Why is the government making so much of the foreign visitors?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]40 make nonsense of показать бессмысленность, ненужность и т. п. (чего-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ His wounded leg made nonsense of his claim to have run five miles. The examination system is made nonsense of if people cheat.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]41 make a note of сделать запись, записать, отметить; заметить:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Make a note of that man's name, he'll be put on a charge. Will all members please make a note of the date of our next meeting. I made a careful note of where I had left the bag, so as to be sure to find it on my return.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]42 make nothing of:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а не понять (чего-л.), не разобраться (в чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ I can make nothing of his request,[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b сделать с лёгкостью, не заметить трудностей, преодолеть без труда:[/trn] 
	(usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ These experienced climbers make nothing of the difficulties of an ordinary climb. This is one of the most difficult pieces to play, yet this wonderful young pianist made nothing of it.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]43 make a nuisance of oneself мешать, раздражать других; навязываться:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Go and play in the field where you won't be making nuisance of yourselves. "Am I making a nuisance of myself?" "No, no, please stay!"[/ex]
	[m1][trn]44 make one of [p] old use[/p] объединяться (в одну группу и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ "It would be worth a journey... to see that sort of people together, and to make one of them."[/ex] (Charles Dickens, [i]David Copperfield[/i])
	[m1][trn]45 make a pig of oneself [p]infml[/p] обжираться; есть как свинья:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Eat your dinner politely, children, don't make pigs of yourselves! I have such a weakness for nuts that I make a pig of myself every Christmas, eating too many at a time[/ex]
	[m1][trn]46 make a point of акцентировать, подчёркивать (что-л.), придавать особое значение, особую важность (чему-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The singer makes rather a point of her high notes, doesn't she? I make a point of always being early for a meeting. Why do you make such a point of rising early?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]47 make a practice/business of практиковать (что-л.), делать (что-л.) обычным занятием:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Do you make a practice of competing with international firms? Teachers make a practice of correcting the children's spoken English.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]48 make a secret of скрывать (что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Why do you make a secret of your feelings? I make no secret of my fondness for nuts.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]49 make sense of быть в состоянии понять (что-л.):[/trn] 
	(usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Can you make sense of what he says? Will anyone ever make sense of the mysterious writing in the cave?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]50 make a show of делать вид (, что согласен, рассержен и т. п.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Father made a show of anger, but actually he was secretly amused by the boy's action. I think you're just making a show of agreeing with me, in order to get some peace.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]51 make a success of преуспеть в (чём-л.), хорошо справиться с (чем-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ We want someone who will make a success of the chairmanship. Gordon has made a success of translating the ancient poem into simple English.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]52 make sure of[/trn]
	→ MAKE SURE OF
	[m1][trn]53 make a trade of обменяться (вещами и т. п.); произвести обмен:[/trn] 
	(usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Will you make a trade of your blue ball for my green one?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]54 make use of использовать, пустить в ход:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Can you make use of some more help in the kitchen? I could make use of a new typewriter.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]55 make a virtue of necessity из обычных поступков или из нужды делать добродетель:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ You always wake early in the morning, so you can't claim it as a moral advantage; I call that making a virtue of necessity.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]56 make the worst of сгущать краски; занимать пораженческую позицию:[/trn] 
