	[m1][trn]2 истратить, разорить, уничтожить:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ He soon made off with the fortune which he had gained when his father died. Those children have made off with the whole cake![/ex] → make away with (3).
	
make on
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 сделать, произвести (что-л.) на крыше, поверхности чего-л. и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + on[/com]\] [ex]♦ Those birds have made their nest on our chimney![/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 заработать на (чём-л.), получить прибыль от (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ With any luck, we might make on the deal.[/ex]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ How much did you make on the house when you sold it? I made £500 on the old painting that I found in the house. You'll never make money on used furniture.[/ex]
	→ lose on (1)
	[m1][trn]3 make an attempt on делать попытку победить, покорить, побить рекорд и т. п.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ British climbers are making another attempt on the world's highest mountain. An attempt will be made on the long-distance swimming record by this brave young swimmer.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 make an attempt on someone's life совершить покушение на кого-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Terrorists have threatened to make an attempt on the life of a leading politician unless their demands are met. A further attempt has been made on the life of the ruler of a South American state.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 make a beginning/start on начинать (что-л.), положить начало (чему-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ A beginning has been made on the building of the new library. When will Tom make a start on his next book?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 make a claim on предъявлять права на (что-л.), предъявлять требование (компенеации затрат и т. п.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ You may make a claim on the firm for the costs of your journey. What claim can the company make on me after the way they have treated me?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 make demands on предъявлять требования к (кому-л.); запрашивать, требовать:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ If the director keeps making demands on the office workers like that, some of them will leave. Too many demands have been made on the supply of coffee so the price has risen.[/ex]
	→ make of (11)
	[m1][trn]8 make an impression on:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а производить впечатление на (кого-л.), позволять составить мнение о (ком-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ His behaviour made a bad impression on the class. The young singer has made a good impression on the public. What kind of impression did you make on the voters?[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b стараться произвести хорошее впечатление на (кого-л.), стараться влиять на (чьё-л.) мнение:[/trn] 
