make out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 выписывать, составлять (чек, документ и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ When you make out the bill, please give me a copy. Cheques should be made out to Wise Brothers Limited. Have you made out your tax return yet? Be quiet, I'm trying to make out a shopping list. (AmE) Do you need help in making out the papers?[/ex]
	→ fill in (2), fill out (1), fill up (2), write out (2) 
	[m1][trn]2 ясно видеть, различать; хорошо разглядеть:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You can just make out the farm in the distance. Can you make out the shape of the ship appearing over the horizon? Looking through the mist, I could make out the figure of a woman standing under the lamp.[/ex]
	\[[com]T5 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ "She soon made out that she was in the pool of tears which she had wept when she was nine feet high."[/ex] (Lewis Carroll, [ex]♦ Alice in Wonderland)[/ex]
	\[[com]T6 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ There's someone outside the window, but I can't make out who it is.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 понять (что-л. или кого-л.); обнаружить, узнать (что-л.); разобраться в (чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ As far as I can make out, there seem to be no bones broken.[/ex]
	\[[com]T1 (simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ I can't make out the meaning of this poem. Can you make out what he is trying to say? I can't make her out, she's a mystery to me.[/ex]
	\[T6 (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ No one can make out how the fire started. He could not make out whether he was in the right city.[/ex] → figure out (2), puzzle out, work out (5)
	[m1][trn]4 получить ответ:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How do you make that out?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 справляться; жить, существовать:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How did you make out with the committee? How did he make out while his wife was away? I'll make out with this old car for another year.[/ex]
	→ get on (6), go on1 (12)
	[m1][trn]6 наладить близкие отношения с (кем-л.); переспать с (кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 (with)[/com]\] [ex]♦ "How did you make out with the pretty girl we met in the hotel?" "Oh, I made out all right!"[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 esp. [p]AmE not fml[/p] преуспеть (в жизни); процветать:[/trn]
	\[L9\] [ex]♦ Whatever profession this young man chooses, I'm sure he'll make out all right. The firm only offers a six-month contract to start with; when we see how you make out, we will talk about the possibility of more lasting employment.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 делать вид; дать понять:[/trn]
	\[[com]V3 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You can't make yourself out to be younger than you are. He's not such a fool as he's made out to be.[/ex]
	\[T5\] [ex]♦ He made out that his car had been stolen.[/ex]
	→ give out (4)
	[m1][trn]9 притворяться, делать вид; стараться доказать, что...:[/trn]
	\[Т5\] [ex]♦ The lawyers tried to make out that Peter had not been present at the accident. Mary has always made out that her parents were rich, but it isn't true.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 дополнить, включить как часть (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The article was included to make out a book.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]11 esp. [p]AmE infml[/p] заниматься любовью:[/trn] 
	\[[com]IØ (usu. continuous tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The park was full of lovers making out on the grass.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 make out a case (against/for) привести аргументы и доказательства (против/в пользу чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The speaker made out an excellent case, but was defeated in the voting. The government can easily make out a good case for raising taxes again. A case can be made out against changing the gun laws. The lawyers made out their case that the prisoner was not guilty.[/ex]
	
make out of
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 делать, шить, производить из (какого-л. материала и т. п.):[/trn]
