make over
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 esp. [p]AmE[/p] переделывать:[/trn]
	\[T1b\] [ex]♦ I'll have to make this dress over, it's all the wrong shape. Human nature can't be made over so easily.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 переделывать (что-л. во что-л. иное):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (into)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The garage has been made over into a playroom. It'll cost a lot of money to make the room over.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 передавать (дом, собственность и т. п. в другие руки):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (to)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Uncle has made over most of his land to his children. Has all his property been made over? He made over his house for use as a hospital in the war.[/ex]
