	\[L9 + ALONG/ON\] [ex]♦ I don't know how he produces any results, the way he muddles along. The speaker was muddling on, and nobody could follow what he was trying to say.[/ex]
	
muddle through
	[p]v adv[/p]
	→ rub through[p] 
	[m1][trn]not fml[/p] кое-как справиться, с грехом пополам довести дело до конца:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ The British usually muddle through somehow.[/ex]
	
muddle up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 [p]not fml[/p] перепутать, смешать; вносить беспорядок:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (with) (often[/ex] pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ My papers are all muddled up, and I was trying to keep them in alphabetical order. I'm sorry I muddled up your names, they're so much alike. I got him muddled up with his brother. I have a terrible headache, and my thoughts are all muddled up.[/ex] 
	-muddle-up [p]n[/p]
	→ jumble up, mix up (2)
	[m1][trn]2 be muddled up [p]not fml[/p] быть сбитым с толку, быть в расстроенных чувствах:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Give Jane time to settle down in her new school, she's sure to feel muddled up at first.[/ex] 
	— muddled-up [p]adj[/p]
	
muddy up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]esp. [p]AmE[/p] измазаться, забрызгаться грязью:[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP\] [ex]♦ You'll get your good boots all muddied up in the garden.[/ex]
	
muffle up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 закутаться, обмотаться:[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP) [ex]♦ “And in his mantle muffling up his face ... great Caeser fell."[/ex] (Shakespeare, [ex]♦ Julius Caesar)[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 заглушать (покрывая чем-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + UP\] [ex]♦ Can the noise of the engine be muffled up any better?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 esp. [p]AmE infml[/p] успокоиться, замолчать:[/trn]
	\[IØ (usu. imper.)\] [ex]♦ Muffle up at the back there! We need some quiet around here! [/ex]→ shut up (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 esp. [p]BrE not fml[/p] хорошо укутаться, тепло одеться:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Better muffle up, it's cold outside.[/ex]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Are the children muffled up against the cold?[/ex]
	→ bundle up (2), wrap up (2).
	
mug up
	[p]v adv[/p]
