	[m1][trn]2 сваливать (вину и т. п. на кого-л.); налагать (обязательства и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Why аге you trying to place the blame on me? Parents place heavy duties on their children. The government has placed another tax on cigarettes.[/ex]
	→ fasten on (2), impose on (1), lay on2 (2), pin on2 (2), put on2 (2), throw on (4)
	[m1][trn]3 place one's cards on the table раскрыть свои карты:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I see that it's time to place my cards on the table; I am interested in this affair because the woman in the case is my sister.[/ex] → lay on2 (5), put on2 (11), set on2 (6)
	[m1][trn]4 place a construction on по-своему понимать, интерпретировать (что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Make sure that you don't place the wrong construction on his remark; I'm sure he didn't mean to be rude. A different construction was placed on the wording of the law by each of the judges.[/ex] → put on2 (12)
	[m1][trn]5 place someone on his/her honour/on oath привести кого-л. к присяге; заставить кого-л. сказать правду или хорошо себя вести:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I place you all on your honour not to cheat while I am out of the room. All witnesses must remember that they have been placed on oath and must speak the exact truth.[/ex]
	→ put on2 (21). etc.
	[m1][trn]6 place one's hopes on возлагать свои надежды на (кого-л., что-л.); надеяться на (кого-л., что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Many parents place their hopes on their children for the future. Don't place your hopes on this job, you may not get it. Jim has placed all his hopes on winning this race.[/ex]
	→ pin on2 (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]7 place something on one side: 
	[m1][trn]а отложить что-л. в сторону; положить возле себя:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ She placed her sewing on one side when the telephone rang.[/ex] → lay aside (1), etc. 
	[m1][trn]b прервать на время (работу и т. п.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Tom placed his new book on one side for a year while he wrote some magazine articles and informative material.[/ex] 
	→ lay aside (2), etc. 
	[m1][trn]с не обращать внимания; бросить привычку и т. п.[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ It's time to place our differences on one side and work together for a common purpose.[/ex]
	→ lay aside (3), etc. 
	[m1][trn]d откладывать (товар) для постоянного покупателя:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I'll place the goods on one side until you have made a decision about whether you want them. [/ex]
	→ lay aside (5), etc.
	[m1][trn]8 place a premium on поощрять (что-л.); давать высокую оценку (чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ In this school we place a premium on hard work and honesty; brains without character and willingness are worthless.[/ex]
	→ place at (4), put at (5), put on2 (35), set at (12)
	[m1][trn]9 place pressure on оказывать давление на (кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The unions have been placing pressure on the government to reduce its limits on wage increases.[/ex] → put on2 (36)
	[m1][trn]10 place a strain on проверить силу и т. п. (кого-л. или чего-л.):[/trn] 
