put down
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 класть (что-л.) вниз, на землю и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[Х9 + DOWN (on)\] [ex]♦ The dinner guest put down his knife and fork with a look of complete satisfaction. He put his heavy bag down on the ground and rested for a few minutes. Just as I put the telephone receiver down, the doorbell rang.[/ex]
	→ lay down (1), place down, put back (2), set down (1), stick down (2)
	[m1][trn]2 опускать (руку, голову и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ The rest of you can put your hands down now, I can't answer any more questions. If you feel faint, it often helps to put your head down between your knees.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [i] (о самолёте и т. п.)[/i] посадить; садиться:[/trn]
	\[X9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ The pilot was able to put the damaged plane down safely in a field.[/ex]
	\[L9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ That looks like a good place to put down.[/ex] → set down (3)
	[m1][trn]4 высаживать (кого-л.) из машины и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[Х9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ Can you put те down at the next corner, please?[/ex]
	→ alight from, etc., set down (4)
	[m1][trn]5 прекращать работу; покидать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + DOWN\] [ex]♦ Put down whatever you're doing and join the party! It's unkind to take someone up and then put him down whenever you wish, without considering his feelings.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 [p]not fml[/p] съесть большое количество (еды); много выпить:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ You'd be surprised at the amount that boy can put down in a single day.[/ex]
	→ pack away (2), put away (2), tuck away (2)
	[m1][trn]7 записывать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Make sure that you put down every word she says.[/ex] → write down (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]8 записывать (покупки на чей-л. счёт):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (to)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I'll take three boxes please; would you deliver them and put them down (to my account)?[/ex]
	→ chalk up (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]9 выплачивать часть стоимости (чего-л.) при покупке в рассрочку:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ You can buy this house by putting 10% down and paying the rest over twenty-five years, at interest.[/ex]
	→ pay down (2)
	[m1][trn]10 запастись (вином, яйцами и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ When his grandson was born, the old lord put down a case of best wine for the boy's twenty-first birthday. I have put down over 100 eggs this winter, so as to have plenty at the cheap price, for cooking.[/ex] 
	—putdown [p]adj[/p] → lay down (5)
	[m1][trn]11 [p]BrE[/p] убивать, усыплять (животное) из милосердия:[/trn]
	\[T1 (often pass.)\] [ex]♦ The dear old dog got so old and ill that it was kinder to have him put down than to let him go on suffering.[/ex]
	→ put away (7), put out of (6), put to5 (27)
	[m1][trn]12 подавлять; заставить замолчать; пресекать:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The people's attempt to win power was quickly put down, and the government regained control. The police are attempting to put down violent crime in the city. We should be able to put the opposing team down in the first half of the game. Tired of being put down by cruel rulers, the citizens planned to defeat them by surprise. Any writer who opposes the government will be put down.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]13 [p]not fml[/p] осуждать; критиковать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Tom's latest book has been severely put down in the newspaper reports. You shouldn't put anyone down for his religious views.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]14 [p]infml[/p] одёргивать, унижать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ He made an unkind remark, intended to put her down; but she refused to allow her spirits to be defeated,[/ex] 
	-put-down [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]15 засевать, засеивать (другой культурой):[/trn]
	\[T1 (in, to, under, with)\] [ex]♦ This year I intend to put the rose border down to vegetables. [/ex]→ lay down (6), lay off1 (10)
	[m1][trn]16 put one's foot down:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]a [p]not fml[/p] нажать на газ, прибавить газу (для увеличения скорости):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ If you really put your foot down we can get home before the shops close,[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b [p]not fml[/p] занять твёрдую позицию, твёрдо решиться[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I shall have to put my foot down and stop this nonsense. The children were allowed to do as they liked until Father put his foot down and made them obey him.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]17 put down (new) roots [p]not fml[/p] пустить корни на новом месте, обжиться:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ It's good to put down roots at last; we don't intend to move from here. She has moved so often that she finds no difficulty in putting down new roots, making friends and finding a place in the society.[/ex] → pull up (9)
	[m1][trn]18 put down one's tools [p]not fml[/p] прекратить работу:[/trn] 
