	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 класть, помещать, ставить (что-л. или ко- го-л. куда-л.), устанавливать (что-л. где-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + in[/com]\] [ex]♦ Put the vegetables in the pan with very little water and heat quickly. I wish to put some money in this bank account. We are having electricity put in the house. Put the eggs gently in the basket. The object of the game is to put the ball in the hole. Putting his hands in his pockets, he whistled a tune. Put your voting paper in the black box. Don't try to put any more furniture in this room. You've put too much milk in my tea. She put the baby in my arms and ran away. We ought to put the children in the back seat, it's safer.[/ex]
	→ fit into (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 помещать, отдавать (кого-л. или что-л. куда-л.):[/trn]
