	[m1][trn]14 put the fear of God in someone [p]not fml[/p] пугать, стращать (кого-л.), слать кары небесные:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I will not have this nonsense from the workers; go out there and put the fear of God in them, so that they obey orders. The new teacher put the fear of God in the class on his very first day, and had no trouble with the children from then on.[/ex]
	→ put into (13), put up2 (2)
	[m1][trn]15 put one's foot in it [p]infml[/p] попасть впросак, сплоховать, «влипнуть», дать маху:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Jane didn't know you were still in town at the time of her party: now you've put your foot in it! Every time she opens her mouth she puts her foot in it![/ex]
	[m1][trn]16 put one's (own) house in order [p]not fml[/p] приводить дела в порядок, наводить порядок в доме:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The chairman has declared that the department must put its house in order before he will allow any additional money to be spent on machinery and paper.[/ex]
	→ set in2 (8)
	[m1][trn]17 put something in jeopardy поставить что-л. под угрозу:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Our chances of winning are being put in jeopardy by frequent illness among the team. The miners' refusal to work has put the nation's supply of coal in jeopardy.[/ex]
	→ place in (9)
	[m1][trn]18 put someone in mind of напоминать кому-л. (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ That tune always puts me in mind of a fine summer day. His voice put her in mind of her father.[/ex]
	→ set in2 (9)
	[m1][trn]19 put something in motion запустить, привести в движение:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ It may be a long time before you hear the answer to your request, but at least we have put the machinery in motion, and it will go through all the usual stages. [/ex]→ set in2 (10)
	[m1][trn]20 put something in a nutshell [p]not fml[/p] чётко и кратко выразить свою мысль:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Interest rates are high, prices are still rising, there is widespread unemployment: to put it in a nutshell, the country is in a very bad state.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]21 put something in order приводить в порядок: 
	[ex]♦ Help me to put the dining room in order before our guests arrive. I hope you have all put your papers in order before we start the meeting. When the doctor gave him six months to live, the first thing he did was to put his affairs in order, so as not to cause trouble for his relatives.[/ex]
	→ be in2 (25a), etc., be out of (19a), keep in (11), set in2 (11)
	[m1][trn]22 put someone in the picture [p]not fml[/p] уведомлять, информировать кого-л. о чём-л.; вводить кого-л. в курс дела:[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ I don't understand what's going on; will someone please put me in the picture?[/ex]
	→ be in2 (26), be out of (20)
	[m1][trn]23 put someone in his/her (proper) place поставить кого-л. на место, осадить кого-л.:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦If the children behave badly while they're staying with you, don't be afraid to put them in their (proper) place. [/ex]→ keep in (13)
	[m1][trn]24 put oneself in someone else's place/ position/shoes [p]not fml[/p] поставить себя на чьё-л. место:[/trn]
