	\[D1\] [ex]♦ What an awkward position I'm now put into — if I say yes, I'm too demanding; if I say no, I'm too proud — either way I lose! You put me into an impossible position with your behaviour at the party. The opposition member's demand for an enquiry has put the government into a difficult position, especially just before the election.[/ex] → place in (4), put in2 (4)
	[m1][trn]7 [ex]♦ naut (о судне)[/ex] заходить в порт:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The ship has just put into the harbour for repairs.[/ex]
