	[m1][trn]9 вкладывать (деньги во что-л.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ People with small savings are advised to put their money into companies offering a low rate of interest but little risk. You need only put a few coins into the collection.[/ex] → put in2 (7)
	[m1][trn]10 тратить (время и усилия на что-л.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ If you put more effort into your work, you'd see better results. I've put many hours of hard work and study into this piece of music, so I'd like to hear you sing it well.[/ex] → put in2 (9)
	[m1][trn]11 put something into action/effect/exccu- tion/practice приводить что-л. в действие, пускать что-л. в ход; осуществлять что-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ It's time that I put my intentions of hard work into action. The new law will be put into effect next Monday. These old rules are rarely put into practice.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 put one's back/oneself into [p]not fml[/p] работать энергично, с энтузиазмом:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Не made а success of the part by really putting himself into it. I shall have to put my back into finishing this writing on time.[/ex]
