	[m1][trn]а тормозить: 
	[ex]♦ The driver put his brakes on hard as soon as he saw the bus, but he was too late to avoid a crash,[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b [p]not fml[/p] замедлить темп, прекратить делать что-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ You can't go on spending at this rate, you really must put the brake on.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]16 put on the gloves [p]not fml[/p] боксировать, заниматься боксом:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ This famous fighter first put on the gloves professionally after he won an important fight at the age of twenty.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]17 put on the heat/screws/squeeze [p]infml[/p] заставлять кого-л. силой, угрозами и т. п.; нажимать на кого-л.; добиваться чего-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Не threatened to put the screws on if we did not agree to his demands. 'The effect was like that of a burning glass. It was an unfailing method of putting on the heat "[/ex] (John Wain, [ex]♦ The Smaller Sky)[/ex]
	[m1][trn]18 put it on [p]infml[/p][/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а преувеличивать что-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ When he talks about his success, I can tell that he's just putting it on.[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b требовать непомерную цену, вздуть цену:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I refuse to shop at that store any more, they are well known for putting it on.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]19 put on a spurt увеличить скорость, рвануться:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Jim could see that he was losing the race, so he put on a spurt in the last few yards, and passed his opponents.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]20 put one's thinking cap on [p]not fml[/p] хорошенько подумать, серьёзно обдумать:[/trn] 
