	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 also put upon ставить, класть (что-л.) поверх чего-л., на что-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + on[/com]\] [ex]♦ Put the plates gently on the table, they are very delicate. He put his hand on my shoulder comfortingly. Putting the child on his back, he continued the long walk home. She put a finger on her lips to signal silence. Our grandparents never seriously imagined that we would be able to put a man on the moon.[/ex]
	→ lay on2 (1), place on (1), set on2 (1), stick on2 (3)
	[m1][trn]2 сваливать (вину и т. п. на кого-л.); налагать (обязательства и т п ):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Why аге you trying to put the blame on me? Parents put heavy duties on their children. The government has put yet another tax on cigarettes. We shall have to put a limit on government spending.[/ex] → fasten on2 (2), impose on (1), lay on2 (2), pin on2 (2), throw on2 (4)
	[m1][trn]3 набавлять (цену): 
	\[Dl\] [ex]♦ The restaurant puts an additional charge on the bill, to cover increased costs.[/ex]
	→ stick on2 (4)
	[m1][trn]4 поправляться, набирать вес:[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ You seem to have put a little more flesh on your face since your illness. If I put another inch on my waist, I shan't be able to wear this dress.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 ставить на кон, рисковать:[/trn] 
	\[Dl\] [ex]♦ Foolishly, he put all his possessions on the result of the card game. How much are you prepared to put on this horse?[/ex] → bet on (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]6 [p]not fml[/p] also put upon беспокоить (кого-л. ), мешать (кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often continuous tenses') [/com]\] [ex]♦ You're sure I shan't be putting on you if I stay for dinner?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 давать (кому-л. работу и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Dl\] [ex]♦ Who are you putting on the special report? "Put none but Americans on guard tonight." [/ex](George Washington)
	[m1][trn]8 put the arm/bite on [p]infml[/p] заставить (кого-л.) выложить деньги:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ We need another £1,000; can't you put the arm on your rich aunt?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 put a bold/brave/good face on смело смотреть в лицо (опасности и т. п.); сделать вид, что ничего не случилось:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ After the failure of his company, the businessman put a bold face on it and began all over again from the beginning.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 put the brake on [p]not fml[/p] затормозить, уменьшить (траты и т. п.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ We shall have to put the brake on our spending, or we shall have no money left at this rate.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]11 put one's cards on the table раскрыть свои карты:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I see that it's time to put my cards on the table: I am interested in this affair because the woman in the case is my sister.[/ex]
	→ lay on2 (5), place on (3), set on2 (6)
	[m1][trn]12 put a construction on понимать, интерпретировать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Make sure you don't put the wrong construction on his remark: I'm sure he didn't mean to be rude. A different construction was put on the wording of the law by each of the judges,[/ex] also put upon
	→ place on (4)
	[m1][trn]13 put emphasis/stress/weight on also put upon подчёркивать, выделять (что-л.):[/trn] 
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ When giving orders, the captain put stress on the urgency of the work. In every sentence that she speaks, she puts heavy emphasis on all the important words. The director put stress on completing the contract on time.[/ex]
	→ lay on2 (6)
	[m1][trn]14 put something on its feet [p]not fml[/p] пускать что-л. в ход, начинать осуществлять что-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ This summer's good trade should put the new business on its feet. The workers must change their ways of thinking if we are to put the nation on its feet after all these struggles.[/ex]
	→ set on2 (8)
	[m1][trn]15 not to put too fine a point on it [p]not fml[/p] честно говоря:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Your father is really very ill and his chances are slight; not to put too fine a point on it, he may not live long.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]16 put one's finger on [p]not fml[/p] прямо указать на что-л.; нащупать больное место:[/trn]
	\[usu. [ex]♦ simple tenses + can, could\] The doctor was able to treat the disease, although he could not put his finger on the exact cause.[/ex] → lay on2 (9)
	[m1][trn]17 put the finger on [p]infml[/p] указать на кого-л., выдать провинившегося:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ How did you know I was here? Who's been putting the finger on me?[/ex]
