	→ get on2 (8), lay on2 (11), set on2 (13) 
	[m1][trn]c [p]not fml[/p] наложить лапу на (что-л.); схватить; изловить (кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The police will soon put their hands on the jewel thieves. I'd like to put my hands on the man who attacked my daughter.[/ex] → get on2 (9), lay on2 (11), set on2 (13)
	[m1][trn]20 put a hex/jinx on [p]not fml[/p] also [p]AmE not fml[/p] put a whammy on сглазить:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ It's as if some evil magician has put a hex on the team: they haven't won once this year, although they have played so well.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]21 put someone on his/her honour/oath привести кого-л. к присяге; заставить кого-л. поклясться, сказать правду, хорошо себя вести:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I put you all on your honour not to cheat while I am out of the room. All witnesses must remember that they have been put on oath and must speak the exact truth.[/ex] → be on2 (16, 21), place on (5), place under (3), put under2 (3)
	[m1][trn]22 put one's hopes on/upon надеяться на (кого-л., что-л.), возлагать надежды:[/trn] 
