put onto
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 класть что-л. поверх чего-л., на что-л.:[/trn] 
	\[[com]Х9 + onto[/com]\] [ex]♦ You need a bigger brush to put the paint onto the wall. When I put my hand onto the shelf, there was nothing there.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 соединять (кого-л. с кем-л.) по телефону:[/trn]
	\[D1 (often simpe tenses\] [ex]♦ I'll put you onto the director; he may be able to help.[/ex] → be onto (1), get onto (6)
	[m1][trn]3 посвящать кого-л. во что-л., выдавать ко- го-л., сообщать кому-л. о ком-л.:[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Who put the police onto our plan? The thieves would have got away with the jewels if their companions had not put the police onto them.[/ex]
	→ be onto (3), get onto (9)
	[m1][trn]4 давать (кому-л.) информацию (о чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Don't go to that shop for your art supplies; I can put you onto a much cheaper one. Thank you for putting me onto a good thing.[/ex] → be onto (4).
	
put out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 вытягивать, высовывать; показывать язык:[/trn]
	\[Х9 + OUT) [ex]♦ Put your hand out, I have a surprise for you. It's rude to put out your tongue at people.[/ex] → hold forth (3), hold out (1), put forth (1), reach out (1), shoot out (2), shove out (1), spread out (1), stick out (3), stretch forth, stretch out (2), throw out (3), thrust out (1)
	[m1][trn]2 вывешивать (бельё, флаги и т. п.); выставлять наружу:[/trn]
	\[Х9 + OUT\] [ex]♦ If it turns fine, I shall put the washing out. I put the garden chairs out when the sun shone, but I soon had to take them in again.[/ex] → take out (1)
	[m1][trn]3 вынимать, доставать (тарелки и т. п.); приготовить (еду и т. п.); выкладывать (вещи):[/trn]
	\[[com]Х9 + OUT (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Shall I put out the best plates? I'll leave a meal put out for you in the kitchen. Please put out my best suit for the governments' meeting.[/ex]
	→ drag out (1), get out (5), lay out (2), set forth (3), set out (5)
	[m1][trn]4 [i] (о растении)[/i] давать ростки, бутоны, побеги:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We thought the bush was dead, but it has already put out some new branches. [/ex]→ put forth (2), send forth (2), send out (4)
	[m1][trn]5 выставлять, выгонять (на улицу):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Troublemakers will be put out. Two families who could not pay the rent were put out onto the street. Put the cat out before you go to bed. [/ex]→ throw out (4), etc., (5), etc.
	[m1][trn]6 посылать, отправлять (кого-л.) куда-л.:[/trn]
	\[T1 (often pass.)\] [ex]♦ The baby was put out to the nurse when the mother had no milk. After many years of faithful service, the old horse was put out to grass[/ex] (- no longer had to work).
	[m1][trn]7 [p] (о судне)[/p] отправляться, пускаться в плавание, выходить в море:[/trn]
	\[IØ (to) \] [ex]♦ The wind was calm when we first put out to sea.[/ex] → put forth (4), put off1 (5)
	[m1][trn]8 прилагать усилия, напрягаться; тратить (силы):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Putting out all his strength, he uprooted the tree.[/ex]
	\[IØ (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Everyone has to put out if we are to be ready on time,[/ex] 
	—output [p]n[/p] → put forth (3)
	[m1][trn]9 предлагать, излагать:[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses) \] [ex]♦ If you can put out a better system, please do so.[/ex] → put forth (5), put forward (2), set forth (2), set forward (3), set out (8)
	[m1][trn]10 выпускать, производить (товары и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The firm has put out an increased number of bicycles this month. This engine puts out more electric current than the other one.[/ex] 
	—output [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]11 издавать, выпускать, опубликовывать; посылать (сигнал бедствия):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ A report has been put out from the government information office about the worsening unemployment figures. The police have put out a description of the jewel thieves, in an attempt to catch them with the help of the public. The sinking ship put out a call for help over its radio.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 выпускать, издавать:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ The printers put out three numbers of the magazine in its first year.[/ex]
	→ put forth (6), send forth (2)
	[m1][trn]13 выключать, гасить:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Put out all fires before leaving the camping ground. Please put the lights out as you leave the building.[/ex] → be out (3), blow out (4), go out (5), keep in (6), let out (6), put off1 (3), etc., snuff out (1)
	[m1][trn]14 вывихнуть (сустав и т. п.); выколоть (глаз):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ I can't play tennis with you this week, I've put my shoulder out. Mind that sharp point, you nearly put my eye out![/ex] → throw out (14)
	[m1][trn]15 выбивать из колеи, выводить из равновесия; беспокоить, причинять неудобства:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Are you sure it won't put you out if I stay to dinner? Say thank you to your aunt; she has put herself out to amuse you while you were ill. Please don't put yourself out, I can do it myself.[/ex]
	\[V3\] [ex]♦ Mother was always willing to put herself out to help people.[/ex]
	→ impose on (3), lay out (8), put about (3), put on2 (6), set out (9), throw out (15)
	[m1][trn]16 выходить из себя; выбивать из колеи:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Не seemed greatly put out by the arrival of the new workers. She never gets put out even by the most difficult matters. [/ex]
	→ throw out (15)
	[m1][trn]17 приводить в бесчувственное состояние; усыплять:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ It was a careless blow, I didnt mean to put him out. This gas will put you out during your operation, you won't feel a thing.[/ex]
	→ knock out (3, etc., 4)
	[m1][trn]18 [p]not fml[/p] спутывать (расчёты и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I didnt know that cheque had been paid in, now that's put my calculations out.[/ex]
	→ throw out (9), etc.
	[m1][trn]19 тратить, вкладывать деньги:[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 (at, to) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Having put out his father's fortune into shares, he was able to live on the interest. Make sure you put out your savings at a high rate of interest.[/ex]
	→ lay out (4)
	[m1][trn]20 [p]not fml[/p] отсылать, отдавать работу на сторону:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We had so many orders to complete that we had to put the work out to other factories, to fulfil the contract on time.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]21 [i] (в крикете и других командных играх с мячом)[/i] запятнать, лишать возможности увеличить счёт:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ А skilful ball from Snow put out the opposing team's prize hope in the first five minutes. [/ex]
	—put out [p]n[/p]
	→ be out (7), etc.
	[m1][trn]22 esp. [p] AmE sl[/p] расплачиваться:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ People who take our free flights to see the property development are expected to put out when they get there. What do you mean no? We've been to the theatre, you've had a good dinner, why don't you put out?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]23 put something out (of action) портить, выводить из строя, уничтожать:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The brave soldier was given the Military Cross for putting three large enemy guns out of action single-handed. Something's put this washing machine out of action again. I'm sending three of you in the night to put out the enemy position.[/ex] → be out of (5), bring into (3), call into (2), come into (5), go into (15), go out of (3), put out of (2)
	[m1][trn]24 put someone/а firm out (of business) вытеснять (конкурентов, компанию и т. п ):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ This slow trade will soon put me out of business. Jim's father's firm was soon put out of business by big competitors. Watch that other firm, or they will put us out.[/ex] → go out of (4), put out of (3)
