put out of
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 выставлять, выгонять из (дома и т. п ):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Put that cat out of the house, I don't want it in my kitchen. When she was rude to me in my own home, I had her put out of my house. The cruel father put his children out of house and home, and made them earn their own living while they were very young.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 put something out of action → PUT OUT (23)
	[m1][trn]3 put someone/a firm out of business → PUT OUT (24)
