	→ put away (7), put down (11), put to2 (27)
	[m1][trn]7 put someone out of his/her misery [p]not fml[/p] положить конец мучениям, страданиям:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ At last the examination results have arrived, and the students will be put out of their misery: it's better to know the worst than be in uncertainty. Tell me the end of the story, put me out of my misery.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 put someone's nose out of joint [p]not fml[/p] расстроить чьи-л. планы; подставить кому-л. ножку:[/trn] 
