	\[X9 + UP\] [ex]♦ Do you know how to put up a tent? Has the machinery been put up ready for the broadcast? I want to put up a fence between our property и nd our neighbour's. The original college buildings were put up in the 16th century.[/ex]
	→ go up1 (6), set up (1)
	[m1][trn]3 выставлять (на обозрение), вывешивать (объявление, списки и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + UP\] [ex]♦ You are not allowed to put up advertisements on this wall without special permission. The examination results will be put up on this board tomorrow.[/ex]
	→ stick up (2)
	[m1][trn]4 повышать (цену):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Rents are fixed and cannot be put up. Many people think that Britain's entry into the Common Market has put food prices up. The government has promised that taxes will not be put up again this year.[/ex] → go down1 (6), etc.
	[m1][trn]5 упаковывать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ Mother will put up a packed meal for us to take on our walk. The farmers put up the apples in barrels. She put up a parcel for her daughter, who was away at college. The medicine is put up in small bottles.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 снабжать деньгами, платить вперёд:[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ If you put up your share, Father will put up the rest.[/ex]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ That's the rule of the game, so put up or shut up![/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 оказывать сопротивление:[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ Don't be defeated without at least putting up a fight. She didn't put up much of a struggle, so I thought she was willing.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 выдвигать (аргумент и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ What argument do you have to put up against that? You have put up a good case, but I still have to decide against you. What excuse can you put up for your actions?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 выставлять на продажу:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ After grandmother's death, the furniture was put up for sale. The next lot I shall put up is a fine set of old pictures.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 останавливаться (в гостинице и т. п.); размещать, принимать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 (at, for, with)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Where can we put up tonight? We can put up at the hotel, or with friends.[/ex]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Can you put us up for the weekend? I can put up two adults, but no children. Yes, I can put up one more person on this seat which folds down into a bed.[/ex] 
	—put-you-up [p]n, adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]11 давать приют, устраивать; ставить (в гараж и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ Is there anywhere for me to put up my horse? You can put up your car in our garage, as it's empty at the moment.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 выставлять свою кандидатуру на выборах:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1b (for)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Do you intend to put yourself up (for the empty seat in the House)?[/ex]
	\[[com]L9 (for) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Do you really intend to put up for that seat?[/ex]
	→ be up for (1), come up for (3)
	[m1][trn]13 выдвигать чью-л. кандидатуру (на должность и т. п.), предлагать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 (as, for)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I know an excellent man whom I would like to put up as the best person for the chairmanship.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]14 конеервировать (фрукты и т. п ):[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ Every summer, Mother puts up a large Quantity of ripe fruit for us to eat during the winter.[/ex]
	→ do up (6)
	[m1][trn]15 вызывать (заключённого) в суд:[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ Put up the prisoners! The jewel thieves will be put up for trial next month.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]16 поднять (зверя, птицу); выгнать из норы:[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ These dogs are often used for putting up birds, for shooting.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]17 [p]infml[/p] устраивать, подстраивать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1a (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ All the office workers believe that the appointment of the new chairman was put up.[/ex] 
	—put-up [p]adj[/p]
	[m1][trn]18 [p] old use[/p] убирать, прятать; вкладывать (меч в ножны):[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ Put up your sword; we are enemies no longer. All this valuable jewellery should be put up somewhere safe so that it isn't stolen.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]19 убирать, ставить (в гараж, в док и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We had to put the car up for the winter, it was not fit to drive in snow.[/ex] → lay up (3), lie up (2)
	[m1][trn]20 put someone's back/hackles up [p]not fml[/p] рассердить, вывести кого-л. из себя:[/trn] 
