reduce to
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 снижать, сбавлять, уменьшать и т. п. (до более низкого уровня или меньшего размера):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + to (often pass., often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I bought the coat as it was reduced to only $29,99. Your speed must be reduced to the city speed limit as soon as you cross the border. Taxes for poorer people should be reduced to an amount that they can afford to pay. The book will have to be reduced to 200 pages, as printing costs have risen so much. If you are to give a talk, try to reduce your ideas to a few points in note form, so that you can speak freely from your notes rather than read out the whole speech. The great fire reduced the forest to a few trees. The whole town was reduced to ashes in the bombing. This crushing machine reduces big rocks to powder. Use your drawing instruments to reduce this three-sided figure to an exact copy a quarter the size. This machine can reduce copies of the original page to half size.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 ограничивать (определёнными рамками), суживать, сворачивать (до каких-л. размеров):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + to (usu. pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The conquered people were reduced to a small corner of their once large country. Business was reduced to local buying and selling when international trading ceased.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 разлагать на (составные части):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + to (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ This substance can be reduced to a single chemical and oxygen, by passing an electrical charge through it.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 выражать в более мелких единицах:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 + to (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ To calculate the cost, reduce the prices to pence from pounds and pence. To multiply these measurements, reduce the feet and inches to inches.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 сводить к (чему-л. целому); упрощать (что-л.) до (чего-л.), превращать в более простые формы:[/trn]
