	—set-to [p]n[/p]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 прикоснуться (чем-л. к чему-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + to (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ She set a finger to her lips to signal silence. He set the whip to his horse to make it go faster.[/ex] → place to (1), put to2 (1), touch to (1)
	[m1][trn]2 поворачиваться лицом (к кому-л.), танцуя кадриль:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Set to your partners, set to your corners.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [b]set the axe to[/b]:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а срубать (дерево):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ We had better set the axe to that old apple tree, it's getting dangerous,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b уничтожить (намерение, план):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ The opposition has set the axe to the government's plans for increasing taxes.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [b]set a (good/bad) example to[/b] показывать (кому-л.) (хороший/плохой) пример:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ His brave action set an example to the whole army. I expect you to set a good example to the younger children.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 [b]set fire/light/a match to[/b] поджигать (что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Setting light to the letter, he made her watch it burn.[/ex] → catch alight (1), place to (3), put to2 (17), set alight (1), set on2 (10)
	[m1][trn]6 [b]set one's hand to[/b] начать прилагать усилия (к чему-л.), начать работать (над чем-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ I thought it was time to set my hand to some serious study.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 [b]set measures to[/b] ограничивать (что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ We have to set measures to our spending if we are to save for our old age.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 [b]set one's mind to[/b] упорно работать (над чем-л.), направить своё внимание (на что-л.):[/trn]
	 [ex]♦ If you set your mind to your work instead of being lazy, you might see some results.[/ex] → put to2 (18)
	[m1][trn]9 [b]set to music[/b] писать музыку (к каким-л. словам):[/trn]
