	[m1][trn]4 [i] (обыкн. в спорте)[/i] устанавливать (рекорд):[/trn]
	\[T1a\] [ex]♦ The young swimmer has set up a new fast time for the backstroke.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 ([i]в полиграфии)[/i] набирать:[/trn] 
	\[T1 \] [ex]♦ You can set up the type by hand or by machine. We can't change any wording once the article is set up.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 приготовить (напитки или бокалы):[/trn] 
	\[[com]T1 (for) [/com]\] [ex]♦ Will you set up the drinks while I look after the party food?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 вызывать (боль и т. п.):[/trn] 
	\[T1a\] [ex]♦ This wet weather sets up the ache in my old wound.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 поднимать (шум):[/trn]
	\[Tia\] [ex]♦ The crowd set up a shout as the winner neared the post.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 [p]not fml[/p] улучшать (чье-л.) самочувствие; восстанавливать силы:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1b (often simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ You need a holiday to set you up again after all that hard work.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 оказывать (кому-л.) помощь или поддержку, поддерживать (кого-л. деньгами); помогать (кому-л.) устроиться:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (as, in, with)[/ex] [/com]\] [ex]♦ Не gave his son some capital to set him up. His father set him up in the furniture trade. We had to set him up with a large sum of money before the firm would take him. It will take a lot of work by the party to set up the young politician.[/ex]
	\[L9 (as, in)\] [ex]♦ It takes money to set up as a lawyer.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]11 провозглашать (себя кем-л.), называть (себя кем-л.):[/trn]
	\[XI (simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Не doesn't set himself up to be an experienced painter, but his work is pleasing to the eye.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 [p]not fml[/p] подставить (кого-л.)[/trn]
	\[[com]T1b (for) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The thief tried to set his companion up for punishment, but he too was caught and tried. I'm not to blame; I've been set up.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]13 [i] (о театре)[/i] расставлять (декорации):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We shall need help in setting up the scenery for the second act.[/ex]
	\[IØ\][ex]♦ Have the stage workers set up yet?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]14 [p]naut[/p] обтягивать; выбирать в тугую:[/trn]
