	\[[com]Т1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Although he was jumping so well, he failed to win the first prize and had to settle for the second.[/ex]
	\[[com] T4 (usu. simple tenses) [/com]\] [ex]♦ The politician's wife has found it difficult to settle for playing a supporting part instead of living her own life. Many women refuse to settle for staying at home. If you can't gain happiness, you may have to settle for just existing.[/ex]
	
settle in
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 осваиваться в новом доме или на новой работе, помогать освоиться:[/trn]
	\[IØ (to)\] [ex]♦ When we've settled in properly, we'll invite all our friends to a housewarming party.[/ex] 
	\[Ill\] [ex]♦ Experienced workers were asked to settle their new girls in, so that they would be working well quite soon after starting.[/ex] → settle down (5), shake down (2)
	[m1][trn]2 [i](обыкн. о плохой погоде или условиях) [/i]начинаться, устанавливаться, наступать[/trn]
	\[IØ1 [ex]♦ Rain settled in shortly before midday and lasted all afternoon.[/ex] 
	\[It + 13\] [ex]♦ It settled in to snow soon after daybreak, and a severe storm covered the whole lakeshore area. [/ex]→ set in1 (2)
	[b]II
	[m1][trn][/b]1 устраивать (что-л., кого-л. или себя где-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 + in\] [ex]♦ Once he settled his body in the comfortable bed, he was soon asleep. It's so nice to sit here and settle my feet in the sand. Settling himself in the chair, he began to address the meeting.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 поселить(ся) (где-л.):[/trn]
	\[IØ + in\] [ex]♦ My family settled in this city over a century ago.[/ex]
	\[[com]IT + in[/com]\] [ex]♦ The people who had escaped from the war were settled in a special camp.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 осваиваться (в новом доме или на новой работе), помогать освоиться:[/trn]
	\[IØ + in\] [ex]♦ How long did it take you to settle in your new home?[/ex]
	\[T1 + in\] [ex]♦ let me get the children settled in their new school first, and then I'll look for a job.[/ex]
	
