	\[L9 + BY/PAST\] [ex]♦ The enemy guns were facing inland, so our ship slipped by without being seen.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [i](о времени)[/i] бежать:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ All these weeks have slipped by, and I've hardly any work to show for it![/ex] → slip away (2)
	[m1][trn]3 [i] (о случае, возможности)[/i] пройти мимо:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Never let a chance to improve your English slip by![/ex]
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 проскользнуть (мимо чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + by/past[/com]\] [ex]♦ You should be able to slip past the open door without the teacher seeing you.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [i](о времени)[/i] проходить мимо (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Sometimes I feel that life is slipping by me, and I've done nothing![/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 пройти мимо (кого-л.), быть пропущенным (кем-л.); пронести (что-л.) мимо внимания (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How did a mistake like that slip by the printers?[/ex]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ You'll never slip an idea like that past the examiners.[/ex]
	
