speak about
	[m0][p]v prep[/p] 
	→ talk about (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]говорить (о чём-л. или ком-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + about (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ We don't speak about that unfortunate period in our family history. Nice people don't speak about such unpleasant matters.[/ex]
	
speak against
	[m0][p]v prep[/p] 
	→ speak for (2)
	[m1][trn]высказываться (против чего-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ+ against[/com]\] [ex]♦ Only a few of the committee members spoke against the plan. The chairman spoke against accepting the suggestion in its present form.[/ex]
	
speak for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 говорить (в течение определённого времени):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + for[/com]\] [ex]♦ Each speaker is allowed to speak for five minutes, and then a vote will be taken.[/ex]
	→ talk for
	[m1][trn]2 поддерживать (что-л. или кого-л.), высказываться (за что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + for (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ How many members spoke for the plan? Mr Price spoke for accepting the suggestion, with some changes. I should like to speak for the boy before you punish him. [/ex]
	\[T1 + for\] [ex]♦ May I speak a few words for the boy before you punish him? [/ex]→ say for (2), speak against
	[m1][trn]3 выражать чьи-л. взгляды, говорить (за кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass.)\] [ex]♦ I speak for my wife as well as myself when I thank you all for your great kindness. You must choose one person to speak for the whole group.[/ex] → answer for (1)
	[m1][trn]4 представлять (кого-л.) в суде:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (no pass., simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Who speaks for the prisoner?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 [b]be spoken for[/b] быть обещанным кому-л.:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Sir, if your daughter is not spoken for, I should like to ask for her hand in marriage. The model that you want is spoken for, but I'll see if I can get another. I'm afraid you can't have these seats—they're already spoken for.[/ex]
	→ answer for (5)
	[m1][trn]6 [b]speak for itself[/b] говорить сам за себя; не нуждаться в дальнейших объяснениях:[/trn]
	\[[com] usu. simple present tense[/com]\] [ex]♦ The sales figures speak for themselves; you can see what a successful year this has been. She said that she was willing to help, but her absence speaks for itself.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 [b]speak for oneself[/b] выражать своё собственное мнение:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Speaking for myself, I find the housing quite satisfactory. He is old enough; ask him: he can speak for himself.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 [b]speak for yourself[/b]! [p]not fml[/p] не решайте за меня!; говорите за себя:[/trn] 
	\[imper.\] [ex]♦“Of course, we all want to hear about Mary's new baby." "Speak for yourself—I'm not interested at all.”[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 [b]speak volumes for[/b] [p]not fml[/p] свидетельствовать (о чём-л. положительном), говорить (в пользу чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Her continued efforts in the face of defeat speak volumes for her courage and strength of character.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 [b]speak well for[/b] служить доказательством (чего-л.), говорить (в пользу чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ His generous gift speaks well for his willingness to help others.[/ex]
	
speak from
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 пользоваться (заметками) во время выступления:[/trn]
	\[[com]IØ + from[/com]\] [ex]♦ Will you speak from notes or can you remember everything you want to say?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [b]speak from the heart[/b] произносить что-л. искренне, говорить от всего сердца:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I speak from the heart when I offer you our deepest thanks.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [b]speak (something) from memory[/b] говорить по памяти:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Speaking from memory, I would say it was about ten years ago. At the next practice I want you all to try speaking your parts from memory.[/ex]
	
speak of
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 упоминать; говорить (о чём-л. или ком-л.):[/trn]
	\[IØ + of (often simple tenses)\] She spoke of the government's plans for the unemployed.[/ex] → talk about (1). etc.
	[m1][trn]2 предполагать (что-л.), говорить (о чём-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ This gift of money speaks of your generosity.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 [b]speaking of[/b]раз мы упомянули о (чём-л. ), говоря о (чём-л. или ком-л.):[/trn]
