take at
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 направлять (какое-л. действие на что-л. или на кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ I took a shot at the passing bird, but missed. You might clear the jump if you take a run at it. If we all take a push at the car, we might get it out of the mud.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 [b]take aim at[/b]:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а нацеливать оружие (на что-л. или кого-л.), прицеливаться:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Taking careful aim at the top branch, I shot it in two pieces.[/ex]
	→ aim at (1), shoot at (1)
	[m1][trn]b нацеливаться (на что-л.), направлять усилия (на что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ You have to take aim at what you want and then be determined to get it. Last year we took aim at saving more money, and succeeded.[/ex] → aim at (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 [b]take someone at a disadvantage[/b] быть в более выгодной позиции по отношению к кому-л.:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Quick to take his opponent at a disadvantage, and rarely making mistakes of his own, the tennis player won the prize in an excellent game.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 [b]take something at its face value[/b] принимать на веру:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Can the chairman's offer be taken at its face value, or is he trying to gain some political advantage for himself?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 [b]take fright at[/b] пугаться (чего-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ This horse is so nervous he will take fright at his own shadow, so be careful.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 [b]take a hand at[/b]:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а присоединиться (к играющим в карты):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Please take a hand at cards, we're one player short,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b помочь кому-л. (что-л. сделать):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ If we all take a hand at digging the garden, it'll soon be done.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 [b]take a look at[/b] осмотреть (что-л. или кого-л); посмотреть (на что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Take a look at this strange object hidden behind the fireplace! Jane has been sick again this morning, so I've asked the doctor to take a look at her.[/ex] → look at (3)
	[m1][trn]8 [b]take offence at[/b] обижаться (на что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Please don't take offence at her manner, she doesn't mean to be rude. She's so sensitive that she will take offence at the most harmless remark.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 [b]take a running jump at[/b]:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а разбежаться для прыжка (через что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ You could jump over the gate if you took a running jump at it.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b [p]not fml[/p] с энтузиазмом браться (за что-л.), часто безуспешно:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ I wish the boy wouldn't take a running jump at every job he does, he never finishes one of them properly. The firm took a running jump at producing these fashionable objects, but they soon fell out of favour and the company lost a lot of money.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 [b]take umbrage at[/b] обидеться (на что-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I'm afraid she took umbrage at your remark, which I know was not intended to be rude.[/ex]
	→ take about2 (3)
	[m1][trn]11 [b]take someone at his word[/b] поверить кому-л. на слово:[/trn]
