	\[D1) [ex]♦ I don't have to take advice from you.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]10 умалять значение (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (no pass., simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ His refusal to accept the prize does not take from his success in winning it. There are a few disadvantages that take from the perfection of the house.[/ex] → detract from, take away from (5)
	[m1][trn]11 понимать (по чему-л. ), узнавать (от кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]D5 + it (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I take it from your silence that you agree. I take it from the director that you are leaving the firm.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 [b]be taken from[/b] [i] (о родственнике)[/i] умереть, оставив (кого-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I'm sorry to hear that your mother has been taken from you at such an early age.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]13 [b]take one's cue from[/b]: 
	[m1][trn]а ([ex]♦ об актёре или музыканте)[/ex] вступать (по какому-л. сигналу):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Take your cue from the lighting change; when it begins to get darker on stage, move across to the window and begin your long speech. We don't have all the music here, and will have to take our cue from the drum beat. We can all rise together if we take our cue from the leader in the front row.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b рассматривать (что-л.) как сигнал к действию:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Taking his cue from the silence of the crowd, the speaker began to attack his opponent.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]14 [b]take heart from[/b] ободряться (чем-л.):[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ In spite of a bad start to the year, the company can take heart from the improved sales figures of the last quarter.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]15 [b]take it from here[/b] [p]not fml[/p] продолжать что-л. начатое, обыкн. кем-л. другим:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I've got the job started, now you can take it from here![/ex]
	[m1][trn]16 [b]take it from me[/b] поверьте мне, я знаю, что говорю:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. imper.[/com]\] [ex]♦ Take it from me, this product will be a success.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]17 [b]take one's pick from[/b] иметь свободный выбор:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ Take your pick from the whole collection, I will give you any piece you choose. Of course that team always wins, they can take their pick from the best players in the country.[/ex] → take of (17).
	
take hard
