	→ care for (4, 5), look after (2), see after
	[m1][trn]b быть осторожным:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The children must be warned to take (more) care of the trains as they cross the tracks on their way to school,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]c [p]not fml[/p] платить (за что-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Here's a £5 note — that should take care of the drinks. Have the tickets been taken care of?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]d заниматься (какой-л. проблемой):[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ This new law should take care of the trouble we have been having with men who beat their wives. Each factory has to have special machinery to take care of dangerous chemical wastes,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]e esp. [p]AmE not fml[/p] подкупать (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ Have the police in this area been taken care of yet?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]f [p]not fml[/p] убивать (кого-л. или животное):[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ You take care of the guard, and I'll warn the other prisoners to be ready. It's all right, the policeman who's been watching us has been taken care of. The dogs are easily taken care of with poison.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 take charge of:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а принять командование, стать руководителем:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ The general was asked to take charge of the whole army. Who is to take charge of this class while I'm out?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b взять (что-л. или кого-л.) под контроль:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Someone ought to take charge of that boy and make him behave properly. The young pilot took charge of the plane when his captain became ill during the flight.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]5 take command of [p] often mil[/p] принять командование:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Every officer should be trained to take command of the ship in case of accident.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 take control of взять контроль (над чем-л. или кем-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ At last the day came when he took (complete) control of the company, by buying all the shares. Take control of yourself, aren't you ashamed? The new government must take control of the country as soon as the election results are clear.[/ex] → have of2 (2), have over (1)
	[m1][trn]7 take a dim/poor view of [p]not fml[/p] не одобрять (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com] often simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ I take a dim view of your action in sending the boy home with no parent present.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]8 take a fancy to привлечь внимание (кого-л). захватить (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ The public seems to have taken a fancy to the play, it's very popular and has had to be repeated.[/ex] → take to (14)
	[m1][trn]9 take heed of обращать внимание (на ко- го-л. или что-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ I do not intend to take heed of your school report as I know that it is a poor guide to your actual improvement. You would be wise to take heed of his advice.[/ex] → give to (12), pay to (4)
	[m1][trn]10 take hold of схватить (что-л. или кого-л):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Take hold of your end of the rope, and we'll pull you up. The child took hold of my hand when he became nervous.[/ex] → catch of, get of (5), keep of (3a), keep on (10), lay of (1), lay on2 (12), lose of (3)
	[m1][trn]11 take (one's) leave of прощаться (c кем-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Now I must take my leave of you. I'm already late.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 take leave of one's senses [p]not fml[/p] глупо поступить, лишаться здравого смысла:[/trn]
	\[usu. perfect tense\] [ex]♦ Have you taken leave of your sense? Do you know what harm that would do to the firm?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]13 take the liberty of позволять себе возможность (сделать что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ I took the liberty of borrowing your pen, I hope you don't mind.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]14 take note of заметить и запомнить (что-л.):[/trn]
