	[m1][trn]15 take notice of:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а обращать внимание (на кого-л. или что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ The children always behave wildly when we have visitors, hoping to be taken notice of.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b слушаться (кого-л.), придавать значение (чьим-л. словам):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ You speak to the boy, he takes more notice of you. You haven't taken notice of my last warning. I see![/ex]
	[m1][trn]16 take the opportunity of использовать возможность (чего-л. или сделать что-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ You should take the opportunity of every job that's offered to you. May I as chairman take the opportunity of thanking you for your interesting talk on cricket. Did you take the opportunity of seeing your aunt while you were in the town?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]17 take one's pick of выбирать (из чего-л. или кого-л):[/trn]
	\[(usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Take your pick of these excellent records at specially reduced prices![/ex] → take from (17)
	[m1][trn]18 take the place of заменить (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ I know that no one can take the place of your own mother, but I'll do my best to give you a good home. What can take the place of lost happiness?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]19 take the risk of рисковать:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ If you buy these shares, you take the risk of losing your whole fortune.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]20 take stock of пересматривать, оценивать (свои дела, возможности и т. п.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Many people in middle age begin to take stock of their lives and to search for new meaning in life. Isn't it time to take stock of your position in the firm and see whether it's worth staying with them?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]21 take а/its toll of уменьшать, подтачивать, ослаблять (что-л.), вредить (чему-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Her last long fever must have taken its toll of her failing health. Last month's severe storm has taken a toll of the value of the fruit crop.[/ex]
	
take off
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 убирать (что-л.), снимать (что-л.), сносить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + OFF\] [ex]♦ I can't take the lid off, it's stuck! Help me to take this handle off. I asked you not to put hot cups on the piano: take them off at once, please! last night's strong wind nearly took the roof off! "Some women can't see a telephone without taking the receiver off."[/ex] (W. Somerset Maugham, [ex]♦ The Constant Wife)[/ex]
	\[[com]L9 + OFF (simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The lid takes off to show the contents.[/ex]
	→ come away (2), come off1 (1), draw off (1), get off1 (1), have off (1), pick off (1), pluck off, pull off1 (1), yank off (1)
	[m1][trn]2 снимать (одежду и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I can't take my boots off, they're so tight! I shall never take off this ring which you gave me until I die. Taking off his coat, he jumped into the river to save the drowning child. A gentleman takes his hat off when greeting a lady.[/ex]
	→ draw off (1), get off1 (1), pull off1 (2), put off1 (1), put on1 (2), slip off (3), slip out of (3)
	[m1][trn]3 ампутировать (конечность):[/trn]
