	\[[com]Х9 + down[/com]\] [ex]♦ The murderer threw the body down the cliff, hoping that it would never be discovered.[/ex]
	
throw for
	[m0][p]v prep[/p] 
	→ knock for (2)
	[m1][trn]throw someone for a loop[/trn]
	[p]AmE infml[/p]
	[m1][trn]а. победить в схватке:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The young man was proud of his strength and ability, but the experienced old fighter soon threw him for a loop,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b. ставить в тупик, разбить чьи-л. аргументы:[/trn]
	\[[com]usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The listener's next question threw the speaker for a loop; he had not expected such informed opinion.[/ex]
	
throw in
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 забрасывать, вбрасывать:[/trn]
	\[X9 + IN\] [ex]♦ Please throw your waste paper in here. A bomb has been thrown in, but it hasn't yet exploded. Will you children hang up your clothes properly, instead of just opening the cupboard door and throwing them in![/ex]
	→ chuck in (1), fling in1 (1), pitch in (1), toss in1 (1)
	[m1][trn]2 [i] (в спортивных играх с мячом)[/i] вбрасывать (мяч) на игровую площадку:[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Which player should throw the ball in when it has gone out of play?[/ex] 
	—throw-in [p]n[/p]
	[m1][trn]3 добавлять, давать в придачу:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ If you buy the furniture, the store will throw in a small television set. All these troubles, and bad weather thrown in![/ex]
	→ chuck in (3), fling in1 (3), toss in1 (2)
	[m1][trn]4 вставлять (замечания):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ There was no need for you to throw in that unnecessary remark. ‘But I did go!' she threw in. Although the argument was fierce, I was able to throw a word in from time to time.[/ex] → put in1 (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]5 [p]not fml[/p] бросать, оставлять (работу, учёбу и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ Jim has thrown in his studies. Why did you throw in such a good job when they're so hard to find? I've had enough of this competition, I'm going to throw it in.[/ex] → give up (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]6 вставлять в (речь, доклад, рассказ):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ In his letters, he always throws in some amusing remark about his neighbour's activities. Don't forget to throw in a mention of the chairman when you give the vote of thanks.[/ex] → put in1 (3), toss in1 (4), write in (1)
	[m1][trn]7 throw in one's cards/hand:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а бросать карты, переставать играть в карты:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I've had enough of this game; I'll throw my cards in and go to bed.[/ex] 
	[m1][trn]b [p]not fml[/p] бросать (какое-л. дело); спасовать:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ I'm tired of trying to write a successful book, I think I'll throw my hand in. [/ex]
	→ chuck in (5), fling in1 (5)
	[m1][trn]8 throw in the towel/sponge:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]a [i] not fml (в боксе)[/i] признать поражение:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Isn't it time the old fighter threw in the towel?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b признать поражение, слаться:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ If you leave the competition now, everyone will think you're throwing in the towel, unless you give your real reasons[/ex] → chuck in (6), chuck up (6), fling in1 (6), fling up (10)
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 забрасывать, вбрасывать (куда-л.):[/trn]
	\[X9 + in\] [ex]♦ Don't throw your shoes in the cupboard, put them in neatly. It's so easy these days to do the washing, you just throw the clothes in the washing machine![/ex] → fling in2 (1), toss in2
	[m1][trn]2 throw dust in someone's eyes [p]not fml[/p] обманывать кого-л.; втирать очки:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ The director is a tricky woman to do a business deal with; she has a way of throwing dust in the customer's eyes, so that he thinks he is getting a better offer than he really is.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 throw something in someone's face/teeth [p]not fml[/p] обвинять кого-л. в чем-л. :[/trn]
	[ex]♦ There's по need to throw his recent failure in his teeth in that unkind way.[/ex] → cast in (4), fling in2 (2)
	[m1][trn]4 throw a spanner in the works [p]not fml[/p] испортить что-л., обыкн. намеренно:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Everything was going nicely with our plans, until my uncle refused his money and threw a spanner in the works,[/ex] also [p]AmE not fml[/p] throw a monkey wrench in the works → put in2 (27), throw into (9)
	
throw in with
	[p]v adv
	v prep[/p]
	→ cast in with, fling in with
	[m1][trn]throw in one's lot with связаться (с кем-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ It's sad to see that he's thrown in his lot with criminals,[/ex] also [p]AmE[/p] throw in with.
	
throw into
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 бросить (что-л. во что-л.), выбросить (ко- го-л. куда-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + into\] [ex]♦ I just throw the clothes into the washing machine and switch it on. The boat rocked wildly, throwing him into the water.[/ex]
	→ fling into (1, 2), hurl into (1), pitch into (1), toss into (1)
	[m1][trn]2 бросить (кого-л. в тюрьму):[/trn]
	\[D1 (often pass.) \] [ex]♦ The criminal was thrown into prison as soon as he was found guilty.[/ex] → fling into (3), hurl into (2), toss into (2)
	[m1][trn]3 привести (кого-л. или что-л. в какое-л. состояние):[/trn]
	\[[com]D1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Your remarks have thrown her into a temper. His speech threw the meeting into confusion.[/ex]
	→ get into (11), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 вставить (слово в разговор):[/trn]
	\[[com]DI (usu. simple tenses)[/ex][/com]\] [ex]♦ I wasn't able to throw a word into the argument the whole time I was there. She sat silently, throwing the odd word into the conversation from time to time.[/ex]
	→ fling into (4)
	[m1][trn]5 бросить (людей на помощь, усилия на что-л. и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ We threw all the men we had into the battle. She tries to throw too much influence into the group's decision. [/ex]
	\[V4b\] [ex]♦ The villagers threw all possible effort into rebuilding the bombed houses.[/ex] → fling into (6)
	[m1][trn]6 throw one's hat into the ring [p]not fml[/p] заявить о своём намерении принять участие, особ. в выборах:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Now that the election of the President is about to take place, how many people have thrown their hats into the ring?[/ex]
	→ fling into (8), toss into (4)
	[m1][trn]7 throw oneself into отдавать своё время, силы (на что-л.):[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ The best cure for unhappiness is to throw yourself into your work. After school, John always threw himself into cricket. Jane really throws herself into learning any new song, doesn't she? [/ex]→ fling into (7), hurl into (4)
	[m1][trn]8 throw something into relief выделять что-л., оттенять что-л.:[/trn]
	\[[com] usu. simple tenses[/com]\] [ex]♦ The reddening sky threw into relief a line of trees on the horizon.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]9 throw a spanner into the works [p]not fml[/p] испортить что-л., обыкн. намеренно:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ The jewel thieves thought they had the robbery perfectly planned, until the day before, when the owner unexpectedly took the jewels to the bank, so throwing a spanner into the works. Government talks with the trade union were going well until the chief union leader threw a spanner into the works by declaring that his group were not prepared to yield on any matter in the talks,[/ex] also [p]AmE not fml[/p] throw a monkey wrench into the works → put in2 (27), throw in2 (4).
	
throw off
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]I стряхивать, сбрасывать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[X9 + OFF\] [ex]♦ Look how the duck shakes its back to throw the water off! He put his hand on her shoulder, but she threw it off.[/ex]
	→ cast off (1), chuck off (1), fling off (1), shake off1 (1), toss off (1)
	[m1][trn]2 сбросить (одежду):[/trn]
	\[X9 + OFF\] [ex]♦ Throwing off his coat, he jumped into the river to save the drowning child. It's good to throw off heavy clothes now that summer's here.[/ex] → cast off (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]3 избавляться (от преследователей):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ If we run fast we might be able to throw the police off. I wish I could throw off these newspaper reporters who are following me everywhere. Jane is having considerable difficulty in throwing off her former boyfriend. [/ex]
	→ chuck off (2), fling off (2), shake off1 (2)
	[m1][trn]4 избавляться (от болезни, привычки и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Will Jane be able to throw off her cold in time for the concert? It's very difficult to throw off old habits of thought. He was pleased to be able to throw off such an unwelcome responsibility.[/ex]
	→ fling off (3)
	[m1][trn]5 победить (соперника):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ This young tennis player will have a hard time throwing off the more experienced competitors.[/ex] → fling off (4)
	[m1][trn]6 выделять (тепло, запах и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ When this material burns, it 	throws off a nasty smell and a lot of smoke. [/ex]
	→ fling off (5), give forth, give off, give out (1), throw out (12)
	[m1][trn]7 легко набросать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I can throw off a poem in half an hour. It shouldn't take me more than an afternoon to throw this article off.[/ex] → dash off (2), etc.
	[m1][trn]8 небрежно говорить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ He threw off a list of things he wanted done, too fast for me to write them down. Be careful what remarks you throw off in front of her, she's very sensitive.[/ex] → put in1 (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]9 esp. [p]AmE[/p] сбить с толку (кого-л. или животное):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (in) (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Pet's go through the river, it might throw the dogs off. Any small interruption is likely to throw off my calculations. Any small interruption is likely to throw me off in my calculations.[/ex]
	→ throw out (9), etc.
	II
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 стряхивать, сбрасывать (что-л. с чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + off\] [ex]♦ The dog shakes all over to throw the water off his back. Angrily, she threw his hand off her shoulder.[/ex]
	→ shake off2 (1)
	[m1][trn]2 throw someone off (his/her) balance:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]а лишать кого-л. равновесия, сбивать с ног:[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ A sudden noise from the crowd threw him off balance for a moment and he fell to his death,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b смутить или удивить (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ The unexpected Question threw the speaker off balance for a moment while he collected his thoughts.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]3 throw someone off guard застигнуть кого-л. врасплох вопросом и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ If you can throw the chairman off guard with a carefully worded question, he may tell us of the company's plans. The prisoner was thrown off guard by a remark from the lawyer, and made a mistake which showed his guilt.[/ex] → catch off
	[m1][trn]4 throw someone off the scent/track/trail:[/trn] 
	[m1][trn]a сбить кого-л. или животное со следа:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Let's go through the river, it might throw the dogs off the scent. Walking backwards in our own footsteps will help to throw the police off the track,[/ex]
	[m1][trn]b сбить кого-л. с толку, пустить по ложному следу:[/trn]
	\[often simple tenses\] [ex]♦ These unrelated events tend to throw the reader off the track (of the story). If the police believe our story, it should throw them off the trail for a time.[/ex] → put off2 (4)
	
throw on
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 подбрасывать (дрова в огонь и т. п.):[/trn]
