	[m1][trn]2 накидывать (одежду):[/trn]
	\[X9 + ON\] [ex]♦ We haven't time to dress, just throw a coat on, over your nightclothes, before the fire gets worse. Throw a dress on and let's go to the party at once.[/ex] → fling on1
	
throw on
throw upon
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 бросать (что-л. на кого-л. или во что-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + on/upon\] [ex]♦ Throw some more wood on the fire, will you, it's getting low. Throwing some money on the table, he walked out angrily. The ship has been thrown on the rocks and is sinking![/ex]
	→ cast on2 (1), fling on2 (1), pull over2 (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 бросать (свет или тень на что-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + on/upon (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Please throw some light on this corner to see if the lost ring is there. After dinner, the office block to the west throws its shadow on our windows, so we don't see the setting sun.[/ex] → cast on2 (5), cast over2 (3), throw over2 (3)
	[m1][trn]3 ставить (себя) в зависимость (от чего-л), полагаться (на что-л.):[/trn]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ I throw myself on your support to help me win this election.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 перекладывать (пину на кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[DI\] [ex]♦ I'm tired of having the blame thrown on me for everything that goes wrong. The jewel thief tried to throw the responsibility on his companion so that he could go free.[/ex] → pin on2 (2), put on2 (2)
	[m1][trn]5 throw cold water on [p]not fml[/p] не поощрять, не поддерживать:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ The children planned to go sailing alone, but Eather threw cold water on the idea because he thought it was too dangerous.[/ex] → pour on2 (2)
	[m1][trn]6 throw doubt on [p]not fml[/p] посеять сомнение (в чем-л.):[/trn]
	[ex]♦ Everyone was prepared to accept the statement until the chairman threw doubt on it.[/ex] → cast on2 (3)
	[m1][trn]7 throw light on [p]not fml[/p] пролить свет (на что-л.):[/trn]
	\[usu. simple tenses\] [ex]♦ Have the police been able to throw any light on the mystery of the stolen jewels yet? "It all came about in a way which is worth recalling if only for the light it throws on our Captain's character." [/ex](Laurens van der Post, [ex]♦ The Hunter and the Whale)[/ex] → shed on (2)
	[m1][trn]8 throw oneself on someone's mercy сдаться на милость кого-л.:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ If the judge finds you guilty, you can only throw yourself on the mercy of the court.[/ex] → cast on2 (4), fling on2 (2).
	
throw open
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 распахнуть (дверь):[/trn]
