throw out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 бросать, выбрасывать (что-л. или кого-л. откуда-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + OUT (of)\] [ex]♦ Climb into the hole and throw the ball out, will you? When the fire reached the bedroom, they had to throw the baby out of the window, where she was safely caught by the firemen. In the crash, passengers were thrown out onto the tracks.[/ex]
	→ chuck out (1), fling out (1), pitch out (1), toss out (1 )
	[m1][trn]2 выбрасывать (что-л.), избавляться (от чего-л. ):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I really must throw out those old newspapers.[/ex] 
	—throw-out [p]n[/p] → cast away (1), chuck away (1), chuck out (2), fling away (1), fling out (2), hurl away (1), sling out (1), throw away (1), toss away (1), toss out (2), turn out (4)
	[m1][trn]3 выставить, выпрямить, протянуть (ногу, руку и т. п):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ She threw out a leg and made him fall. Throw out your chests, men! look like soldiers! He threw out his arms to welcome her.[/ex] → put out (1), etc.
	[m1][trn]4 выставить, исключить (кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (of) (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Two members were thrown out (of the club) for failing to pay the money they owed.[/ex] → be out (14), boot out, bounce out (2), cast out (2), chuck out (3), eject from (2), fling out (4), hurl out (1), kick out (4), pitch out (2), put out (5), shove out (6), sling out (2). toss out (3), turf out, turn out (2)
	[m1][trn]5 выкинуть, выставить (кого-л.) из дома:[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (of) (often[/ex] pass.)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The old lady was thrown out of the house because the owner wanted to pull it down.[/ex]
	→ chuck out (4), eject from (2), fling out (5), kick out (5), put out (5), sling out (2), toss out (4), turf out. turn out (3)
	[m1][trn]6 отклонить (предложение, закон и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ The new law was thrown out when it reached the last stage in Parliament. Why did the committee throw my entry out? I'm old enough to compete.[/ex]
	→ chuck out (5), fling out (6), hurl out (2), toss out (5), turn down (4)
	[m1][trn]7 небрежно сказать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Throwing out an instruction as he left, he rushed from the office.[/ex] → put in1 (4), etc.
	[m1][trn]8 выдвинуть (предложение), предложить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ If none of these ideas are good enough let's hear you throw a better one out yourself! After talking together, the group threw out several good ideas.[/ex] → fling out (8), toss out (7)
	[m1][trn]9 сбить (кого-л.) с толку, привести к ошибке (в чём-л. ):[/trn]
	\[T1 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ The unexpected answer threw the speaker out for a moment. You interrupted me, and threw me out in my calculations. Any small interruption is likely to throw out my calculations. [/ex]→ be out (9), be out in (1), put out (18), throw off1 (9)
	[m1][trn]10 испортить (что-л.), нарушить (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1 (often pass.)\] [ex]♦ Our plans were thrown out by bad weather.[/ex] → chuck out (7)
	[m1][trn]11 [p]mil[/p] укрепить линию обороны (людьми):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ We shall have to throw out a line of experienced soldiers to protect our weak front.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]12 испускать (тепло, запах и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Т11 [ex]♦ The dying fire was throwing out a dull red light.[/ex]
	→ fling off (5), give forth, give off, give out (1), throw off1 (6)
	[m1][trn]13 [i] (в крикете)[/i] лишить (игрока) возможности продолжать игру, попав мячом в его воротца:[/trn]
	\[T1 (often simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ A fielder has the ball: can he throw him out?[/ex] → be out (7), etc.
	[m1][trn]14 травмировать (часть тела):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I can't play tennis with you this week, I've thrown my elbow out.[/ex]
	→ put out (14)
	[m1][trn]15 обеспокоить (кого-л.), выбить (кого-л.) из колеи:[/trn]
	\[[com]Т1 (usu. simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ Не seemed greatly thrown out by the arrival of the new workers. Nothing ever throws her out, she always stays calm and cool.[/ex]
	→ put out (15), etc.
	[m1][trn]16 строить, пристраивать (новую часть к зданию):[/trn]
	\[Т1\] [ex]♦ With the gift of money, the college intends to throw out a new wing for science studies.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]17 throw out the baby with the bathwater [p]not fml[/p] вместе с водой выплеснуть и ребёнка:[/trn]
	[ex]♦ There are some good points to the system; let's not destroy the method for a few faults, or we shall be throwing out the baby with the bathwater.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]18 throw someone out of work лишить кого-л. работы:[/trn] 
	[ex]♦ The serious fire at the bicycle factory has thrown 2,000 men and women out of work.[/ex] → put out of (9).
	
throw over
	I
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 перебросить (что-л.):[/trn]
