throw up
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 подбрасывать, поднимать (что-л. или кого-л.):[/trn]
	\[Х9 + UP\] [ex]♦ Tor hours the boy would stand throwing a ball up and catching it again. The machine threw up great heaps of earth. Come to the bottom of the ladder and throw up the other brush, will you? She threw the window up and shouted to her friend in the street. All the crowd cheered and threw their hats up in the air. The baby used to love being thrown up into the air and safely caught again.[/ex]
