work out
	[p]v adv[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 выйти, выпасть; вытащить, достать:[/trn]
	\[[com]L9 + OUT (of) [/com]\] [ex]♦ There's a piece of dust in your eye but it should work out by itself.[/ex]
	\[X9 + OUT\] [ex]♦ The coin has fallen through a hole in the pocket; I'll see if I can work it out.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]2 подсчитать, высчитать (что-л.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Father is still trying to work out his tax.[/ex] 
	\[T5\] [ex]♦ It didn't take her long to work out that she would soon have no money left.[/ex] \]T6) [ex]♦ Can you work out how much it costs to feed the average family? I'll work out when the last payment will be and let you know.[/ex]
	→ figure out (1)
	[m1][trn]3 придумать, выработать (план и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[Т11 [ex]♦ We must work out a better method of saving paper. We'll leave it to the committee to work out the details of the plan.[/ex]
	\[T6\] [ex]♦ Did you work out how to cheat in the examination?[/ex]
	[m1][trn]4 получать(ся) (в итоге):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ I can't work out this sum.[/ex]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ This sum won't work out. [/ex]
	→ come out (10), get out (15)
	[m1][trn]5 понять (что-л.), постичь смысл (чего-л.):[/trn]
	\[[com]T1 (often simple tenses)[/com]\] [ex]♦ I can't work out the meaning of this poem. The government employs men with special abilities to work out the enemy's secret messages. New students spend hours in the library, trying to work out the system of arranging the books.[/ex]
	\[T5 (usu. simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ This map is wrong, I can't work out where we are. When did you work out that he had been lying to you?[/ex] 
	\[T6 (usu. simple tenses) \] [ex]♦ He could not work out whether he was in the right city. No one can work out how the fire started.[/ex] → figure out (2), make out (3), puzzle out
	[m1][trn]6 решать (задачу), разрешать (разногласия и т. п.), преодолевать (трудности):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ At your age, you should be able to work out your own future. We do have trouble in our relationship, but I feel that we can work it out between us without professional help. Don't worry, I'll work things out. These forces are working themselves out in the Labour Party.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 срабатывать, быть успешным:[/trn]
	\[IØ\] [ex]♦ Did your plan work out? I'm sure things will work out for the best in the end. The book seems to be working out quite well so far.[/ex] → pan out (4)
