yield to
	[m0][p]v prep[/p]
	[m1][trn]1 уступать (кому-л. или чему-л. ):[/trn]
	\[IØ + to\] [ex]♦ The chairman spoke so forcefully that the rest of the committee yielded to his opinion.
	Jane must stop yielding to her desire for chocolate.
	I yield to your better judgment.
	He will soon be forced to yield to his more experienced opponent.
	We shall never yield to a conqueror.[/ex]
	→ give in to (5), give to (24), give up (7), etc., (8), etc.
	[m1][trn]2 отдать (имущество и т. п. кому-л.):[/trn]
	\[Т1 + to\] [ex]♦ At last the citizens were forced to yield the town to the enemy.[/ex] → surrender to (1)
	[m1][trn]3 отдаваться (какому-л. чувству):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ It's best to yield to your grief for a time, then you will be able to deal with your feelings.[/ex]
	\[D1\] [ex]♦ Yielding himself to his feelings of worthlessness, he tried to kill himself.[/ex]
	→ give in to (3), give over to (4), give to (23), give up to (4), surrender to (2)
	[m1][trn]4 сменяться (кем-л. или чем-л):[/trn]
	\[Т1 \] [ex]♦ The long cruel winter came to an end at last, yielding to a gentle warm spring. I'm leaving the firm after all these years as I feel that I should yield to a younger man.[/ex]
	\[DI \] [ex]♦ Her keenness for sport soon yielded place to an interest in music.[/ex] → give to (17), yield.
	[m1][trn]5 подаваться:[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ At last the stiff door began to yield to our efforts to push it open.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]6 поддаваться, уступать (какой-л. идее и т. п.):[/trn]
	\[T1\] [ex]♦ Yielding to demands from the public, the Minister made a statement. Don't yield to pity, or you will lose your independence in the family. You will meet much evil in life; try not yield to temptation.[/ex]
	[m1][trn]7 [b]yield to none[/b] быть лучшим и т. п.:[/trn]
	\[(simple tenses)\] [ex]♦ Our products yield to none in today's world.[/ex]
	
yield up
	[p]v adv[/p]
